ntory guide, listing various components, their model specifications, and required quantities for maintenance and operation.\n\nSince the source material is purely text and a table, no diagrams are included in the summary.\n\n***\n\n## 📋 Detailed Summary: Spare Parts Packing List\n\nThe list contains 14 distinct items, categorized broadly into specialized tools, consumables (like electrode rings), structural components, and user materials.\n\n### 📊 Spare Parts Inventory Table\n\nThe following table provides a detailed breakdown of the spare parts, including the item name, model/specification, and the required quantity.\n\n| Item No. | Item Name | Model No. / Specification | Number (Quantity) |\n| :---: | :--- | :---: | :---: |\n| 1 | Allen Wrench | M3, M4, M5, M6, M8 | 1 each |\n| 2 | Double-Head Screwdriver | — | 1 pc |\n| 3 | Special Scissors For Electrodes | — | 1 pc |\n| 4 | Guider | Φ0.5 | 1 pc |\n| 5 | Guider | Φ1.0 | 1 pc |\n| 6 | Brass Tube | Φ0.5 | 1 pc |\n| 7 | Brass Tube | Φ1.0 | 1 pc |\n| 8 | Electrode Seal Ring | 0-1.0mm | 20 pcs |\n| 9 | Precision Drill Chuck | — | 1 pc |\n| 10 | Machine Foot | — | 1 set |\n| 11 | Water bucket | M16 | 4 pcs |\n| 12 | Balance Bar Stand | — | 1 pc |\n| 13 | Water Retaining Plate | — | 1 pair |\n| 14 | User's Manual | — | 1 pc |\n\n***\n\n### 🔑 Key Data Extraction and Categorization\n\nThe spare parts can be grouped into three functional categories:\n\n**1. Tools and Handheld Equipment (Setup/Maintenance)**\n*   **Wrenches/Screwdrivers:** Allen Wrench (M3 to M8), Double-Head Screwdriver.\n*   **Cutting/Cutting Aids:** Special Scissors For Electrodes.\n*   **Precision Tools:** Precision Drill Chuck.\n\n**2. Structural and Consumable Components**\n*   **Guiding/Support:** Two different size Guiders (Φ0.5 and Φ1.0).\n*   **Fittings/Tubing:** Two different size Brass Tubes (Φ0.5 and Φ1.0).\n*   **Wear Parts:** Electrode Seal Rings (specified for 0-1.0mm).\n*   **Structural Parts:** Machine Foot (1 set), Balance Bar Stand (1 pc