r associated mechanical parts.\n\n#### 2. Technical & Procedural Points:\n*   **Directionality:** The new conveyor belt must be installed according to its marked operational direction.\n*   **Reassembly Order:** The most critical procedural element is following the disassembly steps **in reverse order** when reinstalling the belt.\n*   **Adjustment:** Tension adjustment screws must be used to properly set the belt tension (Step 8).\n\n#### 3. Final Quality Control (QC):\n*   **Inspection Scope:** A mandatory visual and functional inspection must be conducted.\n*   **Components Checked:** This includes the belt itself, pulleys, screws, and all connecting components and loose parts within the work area of the conveyor.\n\n[Page 61]\nThis page, titled **8.2.2 Belt change - Central drive**, is an instructional segment detailing the precise, multi-step procedure for replacing or servicing a conveyor belt drive system.\n\nThe summary is divided into three main parts: **Preparation & Safety**, **Disassembly (Removal)**, and **Reassembly (Installation & Tuning)**.\n\n***\n\n## 📄 Detailed Summary: Belt Change Procedure (Central Drive)\n\n### 🛠️ 1. Purpose and Scope\n**Goal:** To safely and correctly replace the conveyor belt, rollers, and tension settings on a central drive system.\n**Reference:** MISUMI Conveyor Systems Manual (Page 57).\n\n### ⚠️ 2. Preparation and Safety Protocols\nThe initial steps focus heavily on ensuring safety and gathering necessary measurements before any mechanical work begins.\n\n| Step | Action | Key Data / Goal |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Power Down** | Turn off the main switch and disconnect the power supply. | **Safety Priority:** Ensure the conveyor is fully unplugged and de-energized. |\n| **2. Position** | Rotate the conveyor belt unit. | **Movement:** Rotate the conveyor $180^\\circ$ for optimal access. |\n| **3. Documentation** | Mark the relative position of the screws on the frame. | **Crucial Data:** Capture existing belt tension settings and screw positions before disassembly. |\n\n### ⚙️ 3. Disassembly Procedure (Removing Components)\nThis section details the systematic removal of covers, rollers, and old components.\n\n| Step | Action | Components Removed | Notes / Diagrams |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **4. Loosen Adjustment Screws** | Loosen the four voltage adjustment screws. | Initial fasteners. | Allows preliminary movement of the drive mechanism. |\n| **5. Remove Blue Cover** | Loosen the five screws located on the blue cover and remove it. | Blue Cover. | The first major protective component removed. |\n| **6. Remove Yellow Cover** | Place the conveyor on its side to access and remove screws from the yellow cover. | Yellow Cover and associated screws. | Requires specialized positioning (on its side) for removal. |\n| **7. Remove Rollers** | Carefully remove the existing rollers and take note of their placement. | Rollers. | Must be handled gently to avoid damage. |\n| **8. Belt Routing Note** | Document the specific path of the belt around the pulleys. | N/A | **Key Measurement:** Essential for proper reassembly and ensuring no snags. |\n\n### ✅ 4. Reassembly and Tuning Procedure (Installing New Belt)\nThis section guides the user in installing the new belt and properly calibrating the tension.\n\n| Step | Action | Detail / Warning |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **9. Belt Installation** | Install the new belt, paying close attention to the required direction. | **Directional Marker:** Must observe and follow the directional markings printed on the back of the belt. |\n| **10.	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-24 03:23:10	2026-04-24 04:57:36
