, and optimal operation of the conveyor. Users are strictly instructed to consult this manual *before* commencing any operational procedures.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ 2.3 Signs and Symbols: Interpreting Safety Mandates\n\nThe core of the manual details the mandatory interpretation of various safety signals. Attention must be paid to the specific type of warning signal to understand the level of danger and the required action.\n\n### A. 2.3.1 Mandatory Safety Signs\nThese signs indicate required actions or protective equipment that must be utilized to ensure safe operation.\n\n| Symbol/Area | Instruction/Requirement | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Prophylactic Clothing** | Requires appropriate protective garments. | Personal protective equipment (PPE). |\n| **Headgear Use** | Mandates the use of a protective head covering. | Protection from falling objects. |\n| **Use Safety Shoes** | Requires the wearing of protective footwear. | Protection for feet/ankles. |\n| **Eye Protection** | Mandates the use of safety eyewear. | Protection from flying debris. |\n| **No Smoking/Open Flame** | Indicates that combustion sources are strictly prohibited. | Fire prevention. |\n\n### B. 2.3.2 Hazard Signs\nThese signs warn of specific physical dangers present in the working environment, requiring immediate caution.\n\n| Symbol/Hazard | Description of Danger | Symbol/Hazard | Description of Danger |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Electrical Voltage** | Danger associated with high-voltage electricity. | **Danger of Falling** | Risk of injury from objects/people falling. |\n| **Danger of Tripping** | Risk of stumbling or tripping over obstacles. | **Danger of Oil/Grease** | Risk of slip or fire due to fluids. |\n| **Danger of Machinery** | Warning regarding moving or operating equipment. | **High Temperature** | Warning of heat exposure or burn risk. |\n| **Danger of Falling Objects** | Warning of falling debris or materials. | **Live Electrical** | Warning regarding active electrical components. |\n\n### C. 2.3.3 Prohibition Safety Signs\nThese signs explicitly forbid certain actions or entries into restricted areas.\n\n| Symbol/Action | Prohibition | Symbol/Action | Prohibition |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Unauthorized Access** | Entry is strictly forbidden without permission. | **Smoking** | Open flames and combustion sources are prohibited. |\n| **No Dirt/Oil** | The area must be kept clear of contaminants. | **Dirt/Oil** | Warning against depositing waste materials. |\n| **No Eating** | Consumption of food is forbidden in the area. | **Restricted Area** | Defines an area where public access is barred. |\n\n### D. 2.3.4 Instruction Signs\nThese signs give mandatory directions or alerts regarding the general environment.\n\n| Symbol/Instruction | Meaning |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Dangerous Environment** | Indicates an area with inherent risks or unstable conditions. |\n| **Attention/Be Careful** | Directs attention to a potential hazard or point of interest. |\n\n***\n\n## 💡 Summary of Safety Signal Categories (Key Data)\n\nThe system utilizes a structured hierarchy of signals, forcing the operator to recognize the severity of the warning:\n\n*   **DANGER:** Imminent danger; immediate hazard exists.\n*   **WARNING:** Potential danger; accident possible if precautions are not taken.\n*   **CAUTION:** Potential injury; hazard requires attention.\n\n**Mandatory Actions:** The safety signs function as critical guides, ensuring the operator understands not just *what* the hazard is (e.g., voltage), but also *how* to mitigate it (e.g., required PPE, prohibited actions).\n\n[Page 9]\nThis document provides a detailed set of safety instructions and operational obligations for the use of conveyor systems. The summary is structured using tables and headings to categorize the critical data and warnings presented on the page.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-17 08:45:25	2026-04-24 04:57:37
