low is a detailed, section-by-section summary.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ Overview of Conveyor Components\n\n### 🔩 8.6.5 Guide Rail Brackets\nThis section describes mounting hardware used to stabilize and support guide rails for various conveyor systems.\n\n| Component | Purpose | Diagram Details |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Brackets (Standard)** | Used for mounting plastic or metal guide rails. | Shows a bracket designed for standard mounting configuration. |\n| **Brackets (Offset)** | Used for mounting plastic or metal guide rails in an angled or offset position. | Shows a bracket designed for offset mounting configuration. |\n**Function:** The brackets facilitate the stable mounting of the guide rails directly onto the conveyor structure.\n\n### 🔄 8.6.6 Transfer Rollers\nThese rollers are crucial components designed to ensure continuity and smoothness when linking multiple conveyor systems.\n\n**Purpose:** To support the smooth transfer of materials or items between linked conveyor systems.\n\n| Component | Function | Visual Representation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Transfer Rollers** | Support the continuous transfer of materials between separate conveyor segments. | Depicts the roller assembly used for transferring items along a conveyor path. |\n\n### 🛡️ 8.7 Plastic Covers\nThis section covers protective and guide covering components for the conveyor system.\n\n**Purpose:** To cover the transfer route and protect components while allowing visibility.\n**Material:** Transparent plastic.\n**Types:**\n*   **L-shaped plastic covers:** Used for corner protection and guiding.\n*   **U-shaped plastic covers:** Used for straight section protection and guiding.\n\n***\n\n## 🗃️ 8.8 Spare Parts Ordering\n\nThis section outlines the critical procedure and key data required for obtaining spare components for the conveyor system.\n\n### ℹ️ Spare Parts Procedure\nTo ensure smooth maintenance, spare parts must be ordered according to established guidelines.\n\n**Important Note:**\