sical and Chemical Specifications (The Measurements)\n*   **Thick-ness:** The physical thickness of the belt (measured numerically, likely in mm).\n*   **Colour:** The overall belt color (e.g., white, green, black).\n*   **Permissi-ble extension:** Specifies the operational stretch allowance.\n*   **Min. tensile strength / Tensile strength:** Critical engineering metrics detailing the belt's minimum and maximum load-bearing capacity (often noted with units and specific notes like $R3$ or $R5$).\n\n#### C. Performance Metrics\n*   **Friction coefficient (Front side / Back side):** Specifies the belt's coefficient of friction for both the front and back running surfaces (measured numerically, typically a decimal value between 0 and 1).\n\n***\n\n### III. Key Data Groupings and Belt Applications\n\nThe belts are grouped by their function, allowing users to select a belt optimized for a specific industrial process:\n\n| Application Category | Example Part Numbers | Key Material & Color | Core Specification / Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Polyurethane Belt** | HBLT/W, HBLT/G | Polyurethane / White, Green | Used for general, durable conveyance applications (e.g., HBLT/W: White, $1.5 \\text{ mm}$ thickness). |\n| **Polyurethane (Oil/Chemical)** | HBLT/POLT, HBLT/POLG | Polyurethane / White	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-24 04:45:31	2026-04-24 04:57:33
