omponent / Tool | Purpose | Critical Action Point |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt** | Main drive mechanism. | Must be installed with correct directional markings. |\n| **Tension Adjustment Screws** | Controls belt tightness. | Must be loosened before removal (Step 3) and tightened precisely during reinstallation (Step 8). |\n| **Pulley Holder** | Supports the pulley mechanism. | Must be fully unscrewed and re-secured properly (Step 4 & 7). |\n| **Power Supply** | Source of energy. | **ALWAYS** turn off and disconnect the main switch first (Step 1). |\n\n### 🔑 Key Takeaways and Safety Warnings\n\n1. **Safety First:** Always disconnect the power supply before starting work (Step 1).\n2. **Directionality:** Pay attention to the marked direction of the belt (Step 6).\n3. **Handling:** When removing the old belt, exercise caution to avoid pulling the pulleys out (Step 5).\n4. **Quality Check:** A final functional inspection must be conducted to ensure no tools, screws, or loose parts are left within the conveyor work area (Step 9).\n\n[Page 61]\nThis document provides a detailed, multi-step operational guide for performing a **Belt Change on a Central Drive Conveyor System** (MISUMI).\n\nThe procedure is highly technical and sequential, requiring both precise mechanical actions and careful attention to belt tensioning and component orientation.\n\n***\n\n## 🛠️ Detailed Procedure Summary: Belt Change - Central Drive\n\n**System:** MISUMI Conveyor System\n**Operation:** Belt Replacement\n**Total Steps:** 13\n\n### ⚙️ Phase 1: Initial Preparation and Disassembly (Steps 1–6)\n\nThis phase focuses on securing the unit and systematically removing the old belt and covers.\n\n| Step | Action | Key Data / Technical Requirement | Visual Emphasis |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Power Down** | Turn off the main switch. | Must disconnect the power supply by **unplugging** the conveyor. | Safety First (Power Off) |\n| **2. Rotation** | Rotate the entire conveyor unit. | Rotate $180^{\\circ}$. | Position adjustment. |\n| **3. Calibration** | Mark the relative position of the screws on the frame. | Critical for capturing the original **belt tension settings**. | Measurement/Marking. |\n| **4. Belt Access** | Loosen the four voltage adjustment screws. | The belt is designed to come off after these screws are loosened. | **4** screws required. |\n| **5. Cover Removal** | Loosen the five screws on the blue cover. | Remove the blue cover completely. | **5** screws required. |\n| **6. Primary Removal** | Place the conveyor on its side to remove screws from the yellow cover. | Must **hand-hold the rollers** in position to prevent them from falling. | Roller stability is key. |\n\n***\n\n### 💡 Phase 2: Roller and Belt Preparation (Steps 7–10)\n\nThis phase involves accessing and handling the major belt components.\n\n**Step 7: Yellow Cover Removal**\n*   Remove the yellow cover.\n\n**Step 8: Roller Extraction**\n*   Carefully remove the rollers.\n\n**Step 9: Belt Path Noting (Crucial Data)**\n*   Note the precise **belt routing around the pulleys**.\n*   *Purpose:* This recording is essential for the subsequent replacement of the new belt.\n\n**Step 10: Old Belt Removal**\n*   Loosen the belt completely and	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-24 04:45:31	2026-04-24 04:57:33
