e foundational vertical support for the conveyor system.\n*   **Type/Configuration:** The stand is available in various types, specifically mentioning the **H-form** configuration.\n*   **Diagram:** (Visual reference of the upright, structured stand labeled "Support stand H-form").\n\n#### 📐 8.6.2 Mounting Brackets (Supports)\n*   **Function:** Brackets serve as crucial supporting elements designed to attach and stabilize various components to the primary conveyor structure.\n*   **Design:** Multiple designs are available to accommodate different applications and load requirements.\n*   **Diagrams:** (Visual reference shows various bracket types, suggesting adaptability for different mounting needs).\n\n### 🛤️ II. Guide Rails (Guidance Elements)\n\nThe system utilizes two distinct types of guide rails—metal and plastic—to ensure precise, linear movement and alignment of materials.\n\n#### 🔩 8.6.3 Metal Guide Rails\n*   **Purpose:** Used for linearly aligning conveyor materials that require metal guidance.\n*   **Application:** These rails are designed to be mounted to the frame of the conveyor.\n*   **Available Styles (Diagram/Types):**\n    *   **Z-form:** Guide rails designed with a distinctive 'Z' profile.\n    *   **Straight form:** Guide rails with a standard straight profile.\n    *   **Y-shape:** Guide rails designed with a 'Y' profile.\n\n#### 🧴 8.6.4 Plastic Guide Rails\n*   **Purpose:** Used for linearly aligning conveyor materials that require plastic guidance (better suited for delicate or non-metallic items).\n*   **Application:** Like the metal version, these rails are mounted to the frame of the conveyor.\n*   **Available Styles (Diagram/Types):**\n    *   **Z-form:** Plastic guide rails with a distinctive 'Z' profile.\n    *   **Straight form:** Plastic guide rails with a standard straight profile.\n    *   **Y-shape:** Plastic guide rails designed with a 'Y' profile.\n\n***\n\n### 📊 Key Data and Component Summary Table\n\n| Component Type | Section 