ves as the electrode. This copper electrode is driven in a controlled **vertical up and down motion** against the target metal workpiece. The drilling action is achieved through the controlled passage of electrical sparks (spark discharge), which rapidly erodes the metal material to form a hole.\n\n### II. Key Data and Technical Specifications (Table Format)\n\n| Attribute | Detail | Description / Function |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Machine Model** | DK-908 | The specific designation for the EDM Hole Drilling apparatus. |\n| **Operation Type** | EDM (Electro Discharge Machining) | Non-contact material removal process using electric sparks. |\n| **Process Goal** | Hole Drilling | Creating precise bore holes in metal materials. |\n| **Electrode Material** | Copper Tube (Thin Metal) | The consumable electrode used for machining. |\n| **Movement Pattern** | Vertical Up and Down | Defines the controlled feed and retraction motion of the electrode. |\n| **Energy Source** | Spark Discharge | The mechanism by which material removal (erosion) occurs. |\n| **Scope of Manual** | Entire Process & Maintenance | Indicates that the accompanying manual covers setup, operation, and upkeep. |\n\n### III. Detailed Diagrammatic Analysis (Diagram Inclusion)\n\nThe page features one large, highly technical **line diagram** that illustrates the physical setup and operational components of the DK-908 machine. This diagram is the core visual representation and shows the integration of multiple systems.\n\n**Structure Description:**\n\n1.  **The Main Processing Unit:** This is the largest component, housing the working mechanism and the electrodes. It features the primary drilling head assembly.\n2.  **The Control System:** Located on the right side, the control panel is visible, indicating the integration of controls for power, feed rate, voltage, and process parameters.\n3.  **Power and Connection Points:** The diagram shows various input ports, cables, and connection points, confirming that the machine is electrically powered and requires complex peripheral connections for operation.\n4.  **The Working Mechanism:** The central vertical assembly depicts the physical trajectory of the electrode (the copper tube) as it moves up and down to perform the drilling action.\n\n**Interpretation:** The diagram confirms that the DK-908 is a sophisticated, integrated system requiring careful mechanical and electrical setup, supporting the manual's claim that it covers the "Entire Process."\n\n### IV. Summary Synthesis (Conclusion)\n\nIn summary, the DK-908 is a dedicated industrial tool utilizing the electro-discharge principle for drilling precision holes. Its efficiency relies on the controlled vertical movement of a copper electrode which achieves material removal through intense electrical sparking. The accompanying documentation (implied by the footer) is comprehensive, guiding the operator through the entire lifecycle of the machine—from initial setup and operation to routine maintenance.\n\n[Page 5]\nThis page, titled **"2. MACHINE COMPOSITION"** and **"MACHINE EXTERNAL IDENTIFICATION DIAGRAM,"** provides a detailed technical breakdown and schematic view of a complex industrial machine. The document’s primary purpose is to identify and list all the structural and functional components that make up the complete operational unit.\n\nSince the content is highly illustrative, the summary is structured using a **System Overview, Component Table,** and a **Diagrammatic Description** to capture all the required detail.\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Detailed Summary: Machine Composition\n\n### I. System Overview and Introduction\n\nThe document establishes that the machine is a composite system, meaning it is assembled from several major subsystems. According to the introductory text, the machine is mainly composed of:\n\n1.  **Machine Head:** The primary operational component.\n2.  **Box Part:** The main structural housing/base.\n3.  **Working Fluid Supply Unit:** Component responsible for providing necessary fluids/pressure.\n4	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-24 03:35:25	2026-04-24 04:57:35
