** The core function is feedback-driven. The control unit continuously adjusts the pulse signal based on the **difference** between:\n    *   The **given value** (the desired setting).\n    *   The **actual running value** (reported by the feedback signal).\n*   **Power Delivery:** The power driving unit acts as the main loop of the system.\n*   **Output Control:** The pulse signal is converted into the corresponding **angular displacement** on the stepper motor.\n*   **Adjustability:** The speed of the stepper motor can be adjusted dynamically.\n\n---\n### 💡 Key Takeaways (Summary Checklist)\n\n*   **Input Power:** Managed by the **Rectifier Unit**.\n*   **Power Control:** **Pulse Power Supply** governs the distribution of electrical pulses.\n*   **Motor Control:** The **Spindle Servo System** provides closed-loop feedback, ensuring accuracy.\n*   **Core Principle:** The servo system constantly minimizes the error by comparing the *desired* state vs. the *actual* state.\n*   **Output Mechanism:** The final command is converted by the system into angular displacement via the **Stepper Motor**.\n\n[Page 19]\nThis page provides a technical description and diagram of a highly specialized device called the **Rotating Head**, detailing its function, operational mechanisms, and technical advantages.\n\nBelow is a detailed summary organized by function, technical specifications, and component breakdown.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ Summary: Rotating Head (Section 5.2)\n\n### I. Operational Overview and Function\nThe Rotating Head is an integrated design mounted on a spindle slider. Its primary purpose is to facilitate the **sealing introduction of high-pressure working fluid** during various electro-chemical processes.\n\n**Core Functions:**\n*   **Process Application:** It is actively used during clamping, rotation, conduction, and the rotation of the copper tube electrode.\n*   **Mechanism:** The rotation of the copper tube is directly driven by the motor.\n*   **Fluid Management:** High-pressure working fluid is injected into the central hole of the rotor.\n\n### II. Key Technical Features and Advantages (Key Data)\n\nThe design emphasizes reliability, efficiency, and adjustability.\n\n| Feature | Specification / Advantage | Significance |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Fluid Introduction** | High-pressure working fluid injection into the central hole of the rotor. | Ensures effective material interaction and sealing. |\n| **Design Reliability** | Excellent water leakage prevention performance and a more reasonable structure for the sealed water inlet device. | Enhances durability and operational safety. |\n| **Motor Drive** | Rotation is directly driven by the motor (Synchronous gear reduction drive is omitted in the middle). | Provides efficient and direct torque transmission. |\n| **Performance Metrics** | **Wide** voltage adjustment range; **Large** torque; **Low** failure rate; Adjustable rotation speed. | Provides maximum operational flexibility and reliability. |\n\n### III. Component Diagram Breakdown\n\nThe accompanying diagram illustrates the physical structure of the rotating head, detailing key components involved in the fluid introduction and rotation process.\n\n#### 📐 Diagram Components (Labeled Key Data)\n\n*   **Rotary Motor:** The primary power source for rotation.\n*   **High Pressure Inlet Pipe:** The conduit through which the high-pressure working fluid is introduced into the system.\n*   **Return Pipe:** Manages the path of the fluid after its use within the rotor chamber.\n*   **Sealed Waterproof Device:** A critical component ensuring that the system maintains an airtight seal while operating under high pressure.\n*   **Carbon Brush:** A component utilized in the motor system for electrical conductivity.\n*   **Water Spray Outlet:** The point where the processed fluid or working fluid exits the device.\n\n### IV. Legal and	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-24 03:35:25	2026-04-24 04:57:35
