 43, 36, and 63)\n\n[Page 39]\nThis document provides a detailed summary of the conveyance systems offered by MISUMI, covering the types of belts available, operational safety guidelines, and specific technical data for three different belt formats (Flat, Timing, and Plastic Chains).\n\n***\n\n## 🟢 1. Overview of Conveying Belts (4.4)\n\nThe system uses various belts, and selection depends on the application, operating conditions, and required performance.\n\n### ⚙️ Types and Applications of Belts\n\nThe document outlines six primary types of belts used for various industrial applications:\n\n| Belt Type | Application | Illustration/Function |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Flat Belt** | General purpose, sliding, clean industrial processes, thin fluid conveyance. | Standard, smooth belt surface. |\n| **Stainless Steel Belt** | All-purpose, sliding. | High durability and corrosion resistance (implied). |\n| **Timing Belts** | Transport of workpieces. | Toothed mechanism for precise synchronization and grip. |\n| **Plastic Chain** | Transport of workpieces. | Chain-like structure, often used for light load workpieces. |\n| **Flat Belt with Studs** | Transport of foodstuffs. | Specialized surface for handling delicate materials. |\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ 2. Installation and Operation Guidelines\n\nTwo critical safety and operational warnings are provided:\n\n### A. Damaging the Conveyor Belt\n*   **Causes of Damage:** Improper use, over-stressing, bending, or inadequate guidance.\n*   **Action:** Users must take care to prevent damage by ensuring proper alignment and using designated pulleys/guidance rollers.\n\n### B. General Caution\n*   **Safety:** Do not operate the belt if there is excessive damage or signs of wear.\n*   **Guidance:** Only use pulleys and guidance rollers specified by the manufacturer.\n\n***\n\n## 📊 3. Technical Data Specifications\n\nThe document provides detailed technical data for three distinct belt categories: Flat Belts, Timing Belts, and Plastic Cha