gulator terminals.\n\n*   **Direction Rule:** By changing the connection of the motor terminals (relative to the regulator), the operator can reverse the motor's rotation.\n*   **Phase Connection:** The motor connections involve specific terminals for Line (L), Neutral (N), and the motor output wires.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Connection Diagrams and Specific Instructions\n\nThe page features three major wiring scenarios, each illustrating a specific motor type and power range.\n\n#### 1. Oriental Motor Manufacturer B Connection (General)\n\nThis top diagram establishes the basic connection points for a motor to a controller, emphasizing the required phase wires (L, N) and the dedicated ground (PE) connection.\n\n*   **Key Takeaway:** The motor connections utilize separate terminals for the line, neutral, and ground, ensuring a systematic installation process.\n\n#### 2. Induction Motor Connection (6W–25W–40W–60W, 1-phase)\n\nThis diagram is highly technical and shows the physical connection setup using a dedicated capacitor.\n\n*   **Wiring Detail:** The motor wires connect directly to the regulator terminals.\n*   **Capacitor Connection:** The capacitor is connected in the circuit to support the 1-phase operation.\n*   **Grounding:** A clear connection is shown from the motor housing/regulator chassis to the dedicated ground line (PE).\n\n#### 3. Variable Speed Motor Connection (60W–90W–135W, 1-phase)\n\nThis section represents a more robust, variable speed application and shows the wiring layout again, confirming the method for controlling speed and direction.\n\n*   **Connection Method:** The motor is connected to the regulator.\n*   **Grounding:** The ground wire must be connected to the designated ground point (PE).\n*   **Capacitor Placement:** The capacitor is installed with clear connection points, ensuring the motor operates optimally in 1-phase mode.\n\n---\n\n### ⚙️ Summary Table: Connection Rules and Operational Notes\n\n| Parameter | Requirement/Instruction | Safety/Operation Note |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Voltage/Frequency** | Standard operation is at **230V / 50Hz**. | Verify the motor rating matches the system voltage. |\n| **Wiring Setup** | Use the L, N, and Motor output wires to connect to the regulator. | Always maintain a dedicated connection for the **Protective Earth (PE)** wire. |\n| **Motor Direction** | Direction (CW or CCW) is determined by the terminal wiring sequence. | Swapping the connections allows the direction to be reversed. |\n| **1-Phase Operation** | A capacitor (**C**) is mandatory for efficient 1-phase operation. | The capacitor must be wired according to the model diagrams. |\n| **Grounding (PE)** | Grounding must be connected securely to the motor and regulator chassis. | **Crucial Safety Feature.** Prevents electrical shock and protects equipment. |\n| **Variable Speed** | The regulator manages the speed, allowing continuous adjustment of the motor's RPM. | Appropriate capacitor use is critical for stable speed regulation. |\n\n[Page 53]\nThis page, titled under the umbrella of **Transportation, Installation, Connection**, provides detailed technical guidelines, torque specifications, model reference data, and dimensional drawings for integrating and selecting conveyor drive motors.\n\nHere is a detailed summary of the content:\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ I. Technical Guidelines and Connection (Section 5.6)\n\n**Topic:** Connection of Third-Party Drives\n\n### Key Instructions:\n*   **Adherence to Specifications:** When connecting third-party drives, users **must** ensure that the selected drives meet the technical specifications detailed in the corresponding manual chapters (specifically referencing Chapter 4.5.1, etc.).\n*   **Safety:** Installation and connection must follow the manufacturer's guidelines to ensure proper function and safety.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 II. Key Data Tables\n\n###	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-24 03:23:10	2026-04-24 04:57:36
