 **4.3.20 CVGDE**. Both models feature a head drive and are designed for belt conveyance, detailing their specifications, operational data, and performance curves.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ Overview and Model Comparison\n\nThe two models differ primarily in their maximum pulley diameter and corresponding belt width suitability.\n\n| Feature | 4.3.19 CVGBE (Left) | 4.3.20 CVGDE (Right) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Application** | Conveyor system (Head Drive) | Conveyor system (Head Drive) |\n| **Belt Type** | Flat belt, single belt | Flat belt, single belt |\n| **Max Pulley Diameter ($\\text{D}$)** | $\\le 30 \\text{ mm}$ | $\\le 50 \\text{ mm}$ |\n| **Primary Belt Width Range** | $150 - 300 \\text{ mm}$ | $50 - 300 \\text{ mm}$ |\n| **Overall Purpose** | Handling medium-sized loads with restricted pulley size. | Handling a wider range of loads with a larger pulley capacity. |\n\n***\n\n## 📊 Technical Specifications (Common)\n\nBoth systems share the following standard operating electrical specifications:\n\n*   **Voltage ($\\text{V}$):** $230 \\text{ V}$\n*   **Frequency ($\\text{Hz}$):** $50 \\text{ Hz}$\n*   **Voltage Range:** $230 \\text{ V}$\n*   **Operation:** Suitable for both $50 \\text{ Hz}$ and $60 \\text{ Hz}$ operation (as indicated by the performance graphs).\n\n### Technical Data Table\n\n| Parameter | 4.3.19 CVGBE | 4.3.20 CVGDE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width ($\\text{mm}$)** | $150 - 300$ | $50 - 300$ |\n| **Length ($\\text{mm}$)** | $190 - 2000$ | $240 - 2000$ |\n| **Weight ($\\text{kg}$)** | $4.2 - 17.4$ | $6 - 25.7$ |\n\n***\n\n## 📈 Performance Data and Diagrams\n\nBoth models feature operational diagrams showing the relationship between load/torque and speed, and the accompanying detailed data tables.\n\n### 1. Torque / Power Graph Analysis\n\n*   **Diagram	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-17 08:45:25	2026-04-24 04:57:37
