 check is critical before assembly.\n\n1.  **Selection:** Select a copper tube electrode.\n2.  **Damage Check:** Ensure the electrode is free from damage or bends.\n3.  **Cleaning:** The electrode must be thoroughly inspected. A simple method is to open one end and blow into the other.\n4.  **Contamination Check:** Inspect for any blisters or debris inside the tube.\n    *   **Key Data:** If the blisters are appropriate (i.e., small, non-critical), no action is needed.\n\n#### B. Assembly and Installation (Diagram Reference)\n\nThe guide structure is assembled onto the machine using the parts shown in the schematic.\n\n**Components Identified:**\n*   Guide Plate\n*   Guide Lock Screw\n*   Electrode Director\n*   Copper Tube Electrode\n\n**Procedure:** The guide components are mounted to receive the copper tube electrode.\n\n#### C. Preparation and Cutting (Section 6.3 - part b)\n\nThis step details how the electrode is cut to the required length for processing.\n\n1.  **General Method:** If the copper tube electrode is suspected to be plugged or obstructed, special attention is required.\n2.  **Cleaning (Sludge/Blockage):** If the tube opening is blocked, gently turn the copper tube and cut the front end of the copper tube using a few millimeters of cutting action.\n3.  **Positioning:** The electrode must be held while cutting (cannot be held by bending or damaging the tube).\n4.  **Advanced Technique:** If the setup is still difficult, it is possible to install the copper tube onto the machine first, and then use a specialized jig or special scissors to cut the end of the copper tube by a few millimeters.\n\n---\n\n## 📐 Schematic Diagram: Electrode Assembly\n\nThe operational setup relies on the following hardware components, mounted on the machine frame:\n\n**(Conceptual Diagram Reproduction based on the visual source)**\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Guide Plate] -->|Mounts To| B(Machine Base)\n    B --> C[Guide Lock Screw]\n    C --> D[Electrode Director]\n    D -->|Receives| E(Copper Tube Electrode)\n```\n\n**Key Data from Diagram:**\n*   **Guide Plate:** The mounting base.\n*   **Guide Lock Screw:** Fastens the guide components securely.\n*   **Electrode Director:** Holds and guides the electrode.\n*   **Copper Tube Electrode:** The primary functional component.\n\n## 📋 Summary of Key Technical Data\n\n| Aspect | Detail / Specification | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Guide Sizing** | Must match the diameter of the copper tube electrode. | Ensures proper fit and stable operation. |\n| **Inspection Data** | Check for blisters, blockages, or bends. | Prevents machine malfunction and ensures material integrity. |\n| **Cleaning Action** | Blow through the tube or use cutting action. | Removes debris and ensures full flow. |\n| **Cutting Precision** | Cut the end of the copper tube by **a few millimeters**. | Provides the precise working length for the process. |\n| **Handling Note** | Cannot be held by bending or damage the tube. | Mandatory safety and handling precaution. |\n\n[Page 25]\nThis page provides detailed instructions for the **(2) Electrode Mounting Method**, outlining the assembly and installation process for connecting an electrode copper tube to a motor chuck assembly.\n\nThe summary is structured into three parts: Component Identification, Detailed Procedure, and Critical Specifications/Cautions.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Overview: Electrode Mounting Method\n\nThis procedure details the sequence for mounting the copper tube electrode using specialized hardware (sealing rings, chucks, etc.) to ensure a secure and functional connection to the motor shaft.\n\n### 📑 I. Component Identification (Diagrams)\n\nThe assembly utilizes several key components:\n\n| Component Name |	unknown_source	[]	2026-04-24 04:57:38	2026-04-24 04:57:38
