neral installation and operation.\n\n### 📈 Performance Diagrams (Graphs)\n\nBoth models utilize two graphs to illustrate performance metrics relative to belt speed. The graphs compare performance based on two common electrical frequencies: $50 \\text{ Hz}$ and $60 \\text{ Hz}$.\n\n#### 1. Conveyor Capacity (Power vs. Speed)\n*   **Purpose:** Determines the maximum material capacity ($\\text{kg/h}$) the conveyor can handle at different belt speeds ($\\text{m/s}$).\n*   **Diagram Format:** $Y$-axis is Max belt capacity ($\\text{kg/h}$); $X$-axis is Belt speed ($\\text{m/s}$).\n*   **Key Insight:** The graph shows distinct curves for $50 \\text{ Hz}$ and $60 \\text{ Hz}$, indicating how operational frequency affects throughput capacity.\n\n#### 2. Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Speed vs. Ratio)\n*   **Purpose:** Shows the relationship between the required operational speed ($\\text{m/s}$) and the necessary reduction ratio of the gearhead.\n*   **Diagram Format:** $Y$-axis is Gearhead reduction ratio; $X$-axis is Belt speed ($\\text{m/s}$).\n*   **Key Insight:** Similar to the capacity graph, the performance data is separated into curves for $50 \\text{ Hz}$ and $60 \\text{ Hz}$, guiding engineers on the correct mechanical gearing to select.\n\n---\n\n## 📑 Summary of Key Data and Differences\n\nThe core function and performance metrics are consistent across both models, but the model designation dictates a major physical difference:\n\n1.  **Model 4.3.29 (Smaller Pulley):** Best suited when a smaller, more compact pulley system ($\\emptyset 30 \\text{ mm}$) is required, paired with a smaller overall unit weight ($4–16.3 \\text{ kg}$).\n2.  **Model 4.3.30 (Larger Pulley):** Designed with a larger pulley ($\\emptyset 50 \\text{ mm}$), which suggests a different operational scale or torque requirement. This model supports a larger maximum length ($3000 \\text{ mm}$) and has a higher maximum weight ($23.9 \\text{ kg}$).\n\nBoth models are highly versatile, offering belt widths from $70 \\text{ mm}$ up to $300 \\text{ mm}$, and operational ranges suited for both $50 \\text{ Hz}$ and $60 \\text{ Hz}$ industrial power supplies.\n\n[Page 31]\nThis page provides detailed specifications and selection charts for two types of Misumi conveyor rollers, **4.3.31 CVSJAE** and **4.3.32 CVSMAE**, along with general operational data.\n\n---\n\n## 📄 Product Summaries & Specifications\n\nThe page presents technical details for two models of flat belt conveyors, each suited for slightly different applications.\n\n### 1. 4.3.31 CVSJAE (Conveyor Roller)\n*   **Special Features:**\n    *   Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n    *   Straight design.\n*   **Technical Data:**\n    *   **Pulley:** $\\text{Ø} 30 \\text{ mm}$\n    *   **Drivetrain:** Center drive\n    *   **Belt:** Features a meandering prevention crosspiece.\n*   **Technical Dimensions (Range):**\n    *   **Belt Width:** $50 - 300 \\text{ mm}$\n    *   **Length:** $220 - 600 \\text{ mm}$\n    *   **Weight:** $6.7 - 14.3 \\text{ kg}$\n*   **Power/Electrical Specs:**\n    *   **Voltage:** $220 \\text{ V}$\n    *   **Frequency:** $50 \\text{ Hz}$\n*   **Diagram:** Includes a graph illustrating the relationship between torque and belt speed.\n\n### 2. 4.3.32 CVSMAE (Conveyor Roller)\n*   **Special Features:**\n    *   Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n    *   Short design.\n*   **Technical Data:**\n    *   **Pulley:** $\\text{Ø} 70 \\text{ mm}$\n    *   **Drivetrain:** Integrated drive\n    *   **Design Benefit:** Reduced conveyor height.\n*   **Technical Dimensions (Range):**\n    *   **Belt Width:** $60 - 150 \\text{ mm}$\n    *   **Length:** $415 - 2000 \\text{ mm}$\n    *   **Weight:** $6.2 - 18.7 \\text{ kg}$\n*   **Power/Electrical Specs:**\n    *   **Voltage:** $220 \\text{ V}$\n    *   **Frequency:** $50 \\text{ Hz}$\n*   **Diagram:** Includes a graph illustrating the relationship between torque and belt speed.\n\n---\n\n## 📈 Operational Charts and Performance Data\n\n### Gearhead Reduction Ra