s.\n\n---\n\n## 📄 Detailed Summary of Conveyor Specifications\n\n### 🟢 Section 1: 4.3.35 CVMBE (Product Overview)\n\nThis model appears to be designed for **flat belt conveyors**.\n\n**Diagram:** Features an enclosed, robust unit shown in black.\n\n**Special Features:**\n*   Flat belt conveyors\n*   Single belt operation\n\n**Technical Data/Specifications:**\n| Parameter | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | 50 – 300 | mm |\n| **Length** | 200 – 2000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 10 – 20 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 25 – 40 | W |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n**Note:** Specifications depend on the overall design of the conveyor system.\n\n### 🔵 Section 2: 4.3.36 CVSTCE (Product Overview)\n\nThis model appears to be designed for **timing belt conveyors**.\n\n**Diagram:** Features a more exposed, streamlined unit shown in silver/metal.\n\n**Special Features:**\n*   Timing belt conveyors\n*   Single belt operation\n\n**Technical Data/Specifications:**\n| Parameter | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | 10 – 20 | mm |\n| **Length** | 245 – 2000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 3 – 7 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 6 – 12 | W |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n**Note:** Specifications depend on the overall design of the conveyor system.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Section 3: Conveyor Performance (Capacity vs. Speed)\n\nThis central section is the most detailed, presenting a performance chart and corresponding data tables that show the maximum **Conveyor Capacity** achievable based on the **Belt Speed** for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz operation.\n\n#### **Diagram/Chart Analysis:**\nThe graph plots Conveyor Capacity (Y-axis, units unspecified but representing load/mass) against Belt Speed (X-axis, 0 to 60). Two distinct curves are shown:\n1.  **50 Hz Operation:** Shows a capacity curve that drops steadily as speed increases.\n2.  **60 Hz Operation:** Shows a similar capacity curve, generally maintaini