duct diagrams, required specifications, and detailed performance tables for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz operations.\n\n***\n\n## 📜 Detailed Summary\n\n### I. General Overview and Common Specifications\n\nThe page is divided into two parallel technical sections for two similar, yet distinct, models of belt-driven conveyors.\n\n**Common Technical Data (Applicable to both models):**\n*   **Belt Type:** Flat belt (conveyors, single belt).\n*   **Pulley:** Diameter ($\\emptyset$) 30 mm.\n*   **Voltage:** 220 V.\n*   **Frequency:** 50 Hz (Primary reference, though performance is also listed for 60 Hz).\n\n**Universal Technical Specification Ranges:**\n*   **Belt Width:** 30 – 300 mm\n*   **Length:** 200 – 2000 mm\n*   **Weight (Range):** 1 – 15 kg\n*   **Power (Range):** 6 – 25 W\n\n---\n\n### II. Product Section 4.3.5 (GVHAE)\n\n#### 🏷️ Key Features and Operation\n*   **Special Features:** Flat belt, pulleys, single belt.\n*   **Drive System:** Head drive.\n*   **Diagram:** Illustrates the belt and pulley arrangement.\n\n#### 📊 Performance Data Tables\nThe tables detail the conveyor's operational capacity based on belt dimensions and frequency.\n\n**Conveyor Capacity Table (Transcribed Data):**\n| Belt Width (mm) | Length (mm) | **50 Hz** (Capacity) | **60 Hz** (Capacity) |\n| :-------------- | :---------- | :------------------- | :------------------- |\n| 15              | 30          | 5.5                  | 6.7                  |\n| 20              | 30          | 7.5                  | 9.1                  |\n| 25              | 30          | 10.3                 | 12.6                 |\n| 30              | 30          | 13.5                 | 16.8                 |\n| 50              | 30          | 25.2                 | 31.3                 |\n| 75              | 30          | 39.4                 | 48.5                 |\n| 100             | 30          | 78                   | 96                   |\n| 150             | 30          | 150                  | 185        