--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Type** | Flat belt | Flat belt | Single Belt, Pulleys ($\\emptyset$ 30 mm) |\n| **Drive System** | Head drive | Head drive | N/A |\n| **Belt Width Range** | 30–300 mm | 30–300 mm | N/A |\n| **Length Range** | 200–2000 mm | 200–2000 mm | N/A |\n| **Power Range** | 6–25 W | 6–25 W | N/A |\n| **Key Difference** | Emphasis on "Head drive" | Includes "Full belt" specification | The technical performance curve and capacity tables are identical. |\n\n**Operational Insight:**\nThe system is highly scalable, allowing manufacturers to select a combination of belt width and length to meet a specific required conveyor capacity and speed, supporting operation at both 50 Hz and 60 Hz frequencies.\n\n[Page 19]\nThis page is a detailed technical catalog section for **Conveyor Systems**, presenting the specifications and operating data for two related models: **4.3.7 GVHNE** and **4.3.8 GVFNE**. The content for both models is highly consistent, presenting a unified system specification.\n\nHere is a detailed breakdown, including diagrams, tables, and key data points.\n\n***\n\n## 📄 Detailed Summary: Conveyor Systems (4.3.7 & 4.3.8)\n\n### ⚙️ General System Overview and Special Features\n\nBoth models describe a robust, central-drive conveyor system designed for continuous material movement.\n\n**Special Features:**\n*   **Belt Type:** Flat belt.\n*   **Application:** Conveyors (single belt).\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\text{\\O} 30 \\text{ mm}$.\n*   **Drive:** Central drive.\n\n**Visual Diagram:** The diagrams illustrate the general components of the conveyor system, showing the belt, the roller structure, and the pulley mechanism.\n\n### 📊 Key Technical Specifications (Technical Data)\n\nThe technical specifications define the physical and electrical limits of the conveyor components.\n\n**1. Dimensional/Material Specifications:**\n*   **Belt Width ($\\text{mm}$):** Range of 30 to 300 $\\text{mm}$.\n*   **Belt Length ($\\text{L}$) ($\\text{mm}$):** Range of 300 to 2000 $\\text{mm}$.\n\n**2. Electrical/Power Specifications:**\n*   **Power Output ($\\text{W}$):** Range of 25 to 90 $\\text{W}$.\n*   **Voltage ($\\text{V}$):** Specified at 230 $\\text{V}$.\n*   **Frequency ($\\text{Hz}$):** Specified at 50 $\\text{Hz}$.\n\n### 📈 Operating Data and Performance Curves\n\nThe page includes two graphical representations:\n\n**1. Operating Graph (Efficiency Curve):**\nThis diagram plots the relationship between **Belt speed/load ratio** (on the X-axis) and a corresponding operational measure (on the Y-axis). The curve indicates the optimal operating zone and the relationship between speed, load, and efficiency for the system.\n\n**2. Speed Ratio Table (Recommended Operation):**\nThis detailed table provides recommended operational parameters for the conveyor, comparing two common frequencies: 50 $\\text{Hz}$ and 60 $\\text{Hz}$. It maps specific loads (e.g., 15, 20, 25, etc.) to the required belt speed/load ratio for both frequencies.\n\n#### Speed Ratio Table Data (Recommended Operational Values)\n\n| Load | $\\text{50 Hz}$ | $\\text{60 Hz}$ |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **15** | 5.7 | 4.1 |\n| **20** | 7.1 | 5.5 |\n| **25** | 8.8 | 6.2 |\n| **30** | 9.4 | 7.4 |\n| **35** | 11.3 | 8.7 |\n| **40** | 13.1 | 9.9 |\n| **45** | 15.7 | 11.3 |\n| **50** | 18.3 | 13.1 |\n| **60** | 21.4 | 16.8 |\n| **75** | 28.2 | 20.2 |\n| **100** | 32.8 | 23.1 |\n| **150** | 45.1 | 31.7 |\n| **180** | 62.6 | 42.5 |\n\n*(Note: The tables for 4.3.7 and 4.3.8 are numerically identical.)*\n\n***\n\n### 📝 Summary of Further Information\n\nThe bottom section provides navigational links for users seeking more detailed knowledge:\n\n*   **Belt characteristics:** Available on pages 43 and 36.\n*   **Accessories:** Available on page 63.\n\n**Conclusion:** The page serves as a comprehensive technical manual, providing not only static measurements (dimensions, power) but also dynamic operational data (speed ratio tables and efficiency curves) essential for selecting and integrating the conveyor system into an industrial setup.\n\n[Page 20]\nThis page provides detailed technical specifications and operational data for two models of timing belt conveyor drives: **4.3.9 GVTSAE** and **4.3.10 GVTSNE**. Both are electric motor units designed for conveying applications, featuring interchangeable reduction ratios based on operating frequency (50 Hz or 60 Hz).\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Detailed Summary of Conveyor Systems (4.3.9 and 4.3.10)\n\nThe document is split into two detailed product sections, sharing similar fundamental technical data but differing in their drive configuration.\n\n### ⚡️ I. Common Technical Specifications (Key Data)\n\nBoth models share the following general technical parameters:\n\n| Parameter | Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 10 | mm |\n| **Cable Length** | 190–2000 / 200–3000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 2.2–5.2 / 2.3–5.3 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 6 | W |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### ⚙️ II. Product Comparison and Features\n\nThe primary distinction between the two models lies in their **drive mechanism** and **overall physical specifications**.\n\n| Feature | 4.3.9 GVTSAE | 4.3.10 GVTSNE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Configuration** | **Head drive** (The motor/drive unit is located at the start/head of the conveyor). | **Central drive** (The motor/drive unit is mounted centrally along the conveyor structure). |\n| **Special Features** | Timing belt conveyors, single belt. Pulley $\\text{\\O} 30 \\text{ mm}$. | Timing belt conveyors, single belt. Pulley $\\text{\\O} 30 \\text{ mm}$. |\n| **Cable Length Range** | 190–2000 mm | 200–3000 mm |\n| **Ideal Use Case** | Applications requiring a concentrated drive at one end. | Applications requiring drive power distributed across the conveyor length. |\n\n### 📉 III. Conveyor Capacity and Performance Data\n\nThe document includes two graphical and tabular representations detailing the conveyor's operational limits: **Conveyor Capacity** and **Gearhead Reduction Ratio**.\n\n#### A. Conveyor Capacity (Diagram)\nThe graphs illustrate the relationship between **Belt Speed ($\\text{m/min}$)** and the **Conveyor Capacity (Load)**. Although the curves are not explicitly labeled with a quantitative Y-axis scale in the visible data, the diagrams show a general trend: capacity is highest at moderate speeds and decreases at very low or very high speeds.\n\n#### B. Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Tables)\nThese tables provide the specific reduction ratios required for the gearhead at different operating frequencies (50 Hz and 60 Hz) and varying desired belt speeds. This is crucial data for selecting the correct drive unit for the application.\n\n**Example Data (Assuming a Target Speed of 3.0 $\\text{m/min}$):**\n\n| Belt Speed ($\\text{m/min}$) | 50 Hz Reduction Ratio | 60 Hz Reduction Ratio |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 5.0 | 30.0 | 36.0 |\n| 10.0 | 20.0 | 24.0 |\n| 20.0 | 16.7 | 20.0 |\n| 30.0 | 12.5 | 14.4 |\n| 50.0 | 10.0 | 12.0 |\n| 100.0 | 5.0 | 6.0 |\n| 200.0 | 2.5 | 3.0 |\n\n***Note:** The reduction ratio changes significantly when moving from 50 Hz operation to 60 Hz operation, requiring careful selection of the drive motor.*\n\n### 🔑 Summary of Key Data Points\n\n*   **Core Function:** Providing timed and regulated motion for conveyor belts.\n*   **Driving Principle:** Both use timing belts and operate with a $\\text{\\O} 30 \\text{ mm}$ pulley.\n*   **Operational Choice:** Users must select between the **Head Drive (4.3.9)** or the **Central Drive (4.3.10)** based on application needs.\n*   **Performance Input:** The selection of the final gearhead reduction ratio is dependent on the required **Belt Speed** and the local **Electrical Frequency (50 Hz or 60 Hz)**.\n\n[Page 21]\nThis page provides detailed technical specifications and operational data for two models of electric conveyor systems: the **4.3.11 GVTWAE** and the **4.3.12 GVTWAE**.\n\nThe summary is organized by product features, fixed technical data, and variable performance tables based on operating frequency (50 Hz and 60 Hz).\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ I. Product Models and Special Features\n\nBoth models describe timing belt conveyor systems, but they differ in the placement of the head drive unit.\n\n| Feature | 4.3.11 GVTWAE | 4.3.12 GVTWAE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Description** | Timing belt conveyors, double track | Timing belt conveyors, single belt |\n| **Pulley** | Ø 30 mm | Ø 30 mm |\n| **Head Drive** | INSIDE the motor | OUTSIDE the motor |\n| **Function** | Conveying material using belt systems. | Conveying material using belt systems. |\n\n## 📐 II. Technical Specifications (Applicable to Both Models)\n\nThe following fixed technical parameters are listed for both the 4.3.11 and 4.3.12 models:\n\n| Specification | Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width (W)** | 50 – 300 | mm |\n| **Length (L)** | 250 – 2000 | mm |\n| **Weight (Kg)** | 3.4 – 8.3 | kg |\n| **Power Output (W)** | 8 – 25 | W |\n| **Voltage (V)** | 220 – 230 | V |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 / 60 | Hz |\n\n*Note: The technical data sheet specifies that "Specifications depend on the design of the conveyor."*\n\n## 📊 III. Performance Data Tables\n\nThe page includes detailed operational data showing the relationship between the **Gearhead reduction ratio** and resulting **Belt speed (m/s)** and **Voltage (V)**, separated by operating frequency (50 Hz and 60 Hz).\n\n### A. Performance Data at 50 Hz\n\nThis table lists operational settings for a 50 Hz power supply.\n\n| Gearhead Reduction Ratio | Belt Speed (m/s) | Voltage (V) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **5** | 30.0 | 36.0 |\n| **7.5** | 20.0 | 24.0 |\n| **12.5** | 16.7 | 20.0 |\n| **15** | 10.0 | 12.0 |\n| **18** | 8.3 | 10.0 |\n| **25** | 6.0 | 7.2 |\n| **30** | 5.0 | 6.0 |\n| **36** | 4.2 | 5.0 |\n| **50** | 3.0 | 3.6 |\n| **60** | 2.5 | 3.0 |\n| **75** | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| **90** | 1.7 | 2.0 |\n| **100** | 1.5 | 1.8 |\n| **120** | 1.2 | 1.5 |\n| **150** | 1.0 | 1.2 |\n| **180** | 0.8 | 1.0 |\n\n### B. Performance Data at 60 Hz\n\nThis table lists operational settings for a 60 Hz power supply.\n\n| Gearhead Reduction Ratio | Belt Speed (m/s) | Voltage (V) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **5** | 30.0 | 36.0 |\n| **7.5** | 20.0 | 24.0 |\n| **12.5** | 16.7 | 20.0 |\n| **15** | 10.0 | 12.0 |\n| **18** | 8.3 | 10.0 |\n| **25** | 6.0 | 7.2 |\n| **30** | 5.0 | 6.0 |\n| **36** | 4.2 | 5.0 |\n| **50** | 3.0 | 3.6 |\n| **60** | 2.5 | 3.0 |\n| **75** | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| **90** | 1.7 | 2.0 |\n| **100** | 1.5 | 1.8 |\n| **120** | 1.2 | 1.5 |\n| **150** | 1.0 | 1.2 |\n| **180** | 0.8 | 1.0 |\n\n---\n\n## 🔗 IV. Supporting Information (Further Details)\n\nThe page references related technical information available in subsequent sections of the manual:\n\n*   **Connection:** Page 43\n*   **Belt characteristics:** Page 36\n*   **Accessories:** Page 63\n\n[Page 22]\nThis page provides a detailed technical overview and operational data for two models of electric conveyor drive systems manufactured by MISUMI. The systems are designed for timing belt conveyors and include specific technical parameters and performance graphs.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ I. Product Overview and Specifications\n\nThe page presents two distinct, yet similar, models of industrial conveyor drives: 4.3.13 GVTWNU and 4.3.14 GVTWNSE. The primary difference lies in the placement of the central drive mechanism.\n\n### A. Model 4.3.13 GVTWNU\n*   **Function:** Conveyor drive system.\n*   **Key Features (Special features):**\n    *   Timing belt conveyors, double track.\n    *   Pulley $\\emptyset$ 30 mm.\n    *   **Drive Placement:** Central drive is located **INSIDE** the motor.\n\n### B. Model 4.3.14 GVTWNSE\n*   **Function:** Conveyor drive system.\n*   **Key Features (Special features):**\n    *   Timing belt conveyors, double track.\n    *   Pulley $\\emptyset$ 30 mm.\n    *   **Drive Placement:** Central drive is located **OUTSIDE** the motor.\n\n### C. Common Technical Data (Key Data)\nBoth models share the following core technical specifications:\n\n| Parameter | Symbol | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | | 50–300 | mm |\n| **Length** | | 280–2000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | | 3.5–8.5 | kg |\n| **Power output** | | 220 | W |\n| **Voltage** | | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | | 50 | Hz |\n\n***\n\n## 📊 II. Operational Diagrams and Graphs\n\nThe page includes several diagrams to illustrate the operating characteristics of the drive system.\n\n### A. Performance Curve Diagram (Upper Left)\nThis diagram shows a relationship (likely between torque/power and speed) plotted against a sinusoidal curve. The axes indicate the relationship between required performance (y-axis) and speed/frequency (x-axis), demonstrating the operational range of the conveyor system.\n\n### B. Operational Graph (Lower Left)\nThis second graph plots operational performance (y-axis, labeled "belt speed / min") against an operational index (x-axis), illustrating the relationship between the belt’s speed and the system’s capacity within the defined operational envelope.\n\n***\n\n## 📋 III. Detailed Performance Tables\n\nTwo large sets of operational tables provide specific performance data based on the required frequency (50 Hz vs. 60 Hz) and the specific belt width being used.\n\n### A. Belt Speed Capacity Table\nThis table specifies the achievable belt speeds for various standard belt widths.\n\n| Belt Width (mm) | 50 Hz (Speed Range) | 60 Hz (Speed Range) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 5 | 30–36.0 | 30–36.0 |\n| 7.5 | 20.0–24.0 | 20.0–24.0 |\n| 10 | 15.0–20.0 | 15.0–20.0 |\n| 12.5 | 12.0–14.4 | 12.0–14.4 |\n| 15 | 10.0–12.0 | 10.0–12.0 |\n| 18 | 8.3–10.0 | 8.3–10.0 |\n| 20 | 6.0–7.2 | 6.0–7.2 |\n| 25 | 3.0–5.0 | 3.0–5.0 |\n| 30 | 2.0–3.6 | 2.0–3.6 |\n| 50 | 1.0–2.4 | 1.0–2.4 |\n| 100 | 0.5–1.7 | 0.5–1.7 |\n| 150 | 0.3–1.0 | 0.3–1.0 |\n| 180 | 0.1–0.8 | 0.1–0.8 |\n\n### B. Gearhead Reduction Capacity Table\nThis table specifies the reduction capacity of the gearhead for various standard belt widths, detailing the operational limits for 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n| Belt Width (mm) | 50 Hz (Reduction Range) | 60 Hz (Reduction Range) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 5 | 30–36.0 | 30–36.0 |\n| 7.5 | 20.0–24.0 | 20.0–24.0 |\n| 10 | 15.0–20.0 | 15.0–20.0 |\n| 12.5 | 12.0–14.4 | 12.0–14.4 |\n| 15 | 10.0–12.0 | 10.0–12.0 |\n| 18 | 8.3–10.0 | 8.3–10.0 |\n| 20 | 6.0–7.2 | 6.0–7.2 |\n| 25 | 3.0–5.0 | 3.0–5.0 |\n| 30 | 2.0–3.6 | 2.0–3.6 |\n| 50 | 1.0–2.4 | 1.0–2.4 |\n| 100 | 0.5–1.7 | 0.5–1.7 |\n| 150 | 0.3–1.0 | 0.3–1.0 |\n| 180 | 0.1–0.8 | 0.1–0.8 |\n\n***\n\n## ℹ️ IV. Further Information\n\nThe bottom section directs the user to other related technical documentation:\n\n**Further Information:**\n*   Connection: $\\rightarrow$ from page 43\n*   Belt characteristics: $\\rightarrow$ from page 36\n*   Accessories: $\\rightarrow$ from page 63\n\n**Further Information:**\n*   Connection: $\\rightarrow$ from page 43\n*   Belt characteristics: $\\rightarrow$ from page 36\n*   Accessories: $\\rightarrow$ from page 63\n\n[Page 23]\nThis page provides detailed specifications and installation information for two specific models of flat belt conveyors: the **4.3.15 CVGAE** and the **4.3.16 CVGCE**.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Overview and Models\n\nThe document outlines the technical specifications for two single-belt flat conveyor systems, highlighting differences in pulley diameter and general electrical standards.\n\n### 🟢 1. Model 4.3.15 CVGAE\n\n**Key Characteristics:**\n*   **Conveyor Type:** Flat belt conveyor, single belt.\n*   **Pulley Diameter ($\\text{D}$):** 30 $\\text{mm}$.\n*   **Drive:** Head drive.\n\n**Technical Data:**\n| Specification | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Bolt Width | $30 - 300$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| Length | $190 - 2000$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| Weight | $4.2 - 17.4$ | $\\text{kg}$ |\n| Power Output | $6 - 25$ | $\\text{W}$ |\n| Voltage | $220$ | $\\text{V}$ |\n| Frequency | $50$ | $\\text{Hz}$ |\n\n**Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Table Summary):**\nThis table specifies the gearhead reduction ratio based on the conveyor's operating frequency and weight/power requirements. The structure shows how different reduction ratios (e.g., 3.1:1, 6.6:1, 13.1:1) are achieved at both 50 $\\text{Hz}$ and 60 $\\text{Hz}$ frequencies.\n\n*(A full copy of the detailed table with reduction ratios is provided in the source material.)*\n\n---\n\n### 🔴 2. Model 4.3.16 CVGCE\n\n**Key Characteristics:**\n*   **Conveyor Type:** Flat belt conveyor, single belt.\n*   **Pulley Diameter ($\\text{D}$):** 50 $\\text{mm}$.\n*   **Drive:** Head drive.\n\n**Technical Data:**\n| Specification | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Bolt Width | $40 - 300$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| Length | $240 - 2000$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| Weight | $6 - 25.7$ | $\\text{kg}$ |\n| Power Output | $6 - 25$ | $\\text{W}$ |\n| Voltage | $230$ | $\\text{V}$ |\n| Frequency | $50$ | $\\text{Hz}$ |\n\n**Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Table Summary):**\nSimilar to the 4.3.15 model, this table specifies the gearhead reduction ratio, accommodating different frequencies (50 $\\text{Hz}$ and 60 $\\text{Hz}$) and load/power requirements.\n\n*(A full copy of the detailed table with reduction ratios is provided in the source material.)*\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Comparative Key Data\n\n| Feature | 4.3.15 CVGAE | 4.3.16 CVGCE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Pulley Diameter** | 30 $\\text{mm}$ | 50 $\\text{mm}$ |\n| **Bolt Width Range** | $30 - 300 \\text{ mm}$ | $40 - 300 \\text{ mm}$ |\n| **Length Range** | $190 - 2000 \\text{ mm}$ | $240 - 2000 \\text{ mm}$ |\n| **Voltage** | $220 \\text{ V}$ | $230 \\text{ V}$ |\n| **Power Output** | $6 - 25 \\text{ W}$ | $6 - 25 \\text{ W}$ |\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Support and Information\n\nThe bottom section acts as a navigational guide, directing the user to further documentation regarding the conveyor system:\n\n*   **Connection:** Information can be found on page **43**.\n*   **Belt characteristics:** Details are on page **36**.\n*   **Accessories:** Supporting parts and options are on page **63**.\n\n[Page 24]\nThis page provides a detailed technical comparison and specification sheet for two models of conveyor systems manufactured by MISUMI: the **4.3.17 CVGNE** and the **4.3.18 CVGRE**.\n\nThe summary is structured to include the models' unique features, general technical parameters, and detailed performance tables.\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Summary of Conveyor System Technical Specifications\n\n### I. Overview of Models\n\nThe systems detailed are **Flat Belt Conveyors** designed for single-belt operation, driven by a central mechanism.\n\n#### 🟢 Model 4.3.17 CVGNE (Left Side)\n\n*   **Special Features:** Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Specifications:**\n    *   Pulley Diameter ($\\varnothing$): 30 mm\n    *   Drive Type: Central drive\n*   **Diagram:** Shows a conveyor unit with a visible central drive mechanism.\n\n#### 🔵 Model 4.3.18 CVGRE (Right Side)\n\n*   **Special Features:** Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Specifications:**\n    *   Pulley Diameter ($\\varnothing$): 50 mm\n    *   Drive Type: Central drive\n*   **Diagram:** Shows a conveyor unit with a visible central drive mechanism.\n\n### II. General Technical Data (Applicable to Both Systems)\n\n| Parameter | 4.3.17 CVGNE (Min - Max) | 4.3.18 CVGRE (Min - Max) | Unit | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 30 - 300 | 40 - 300 | mm | Operational range. |\n| **Length** | 355 - 2000 | 385 - 2000 | mm | Operational range. |\n| **Weight** | 5.8 - 23.9 | 7.3 - 30.6 | kg | Weight range. |\n| **Power Output** | 6 - 25 | 6 - 25 | kW | Motor power range. |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | 230 | V | Standard voltage. |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | 50 | Hz | Standard frequency. |\n\n***\n\n### III. Gearhead Reduction Ratio Performance Data\n\nBoth models include detailed tables showing the relationship between the desired **Belt Speed** and the resulting **Gearhead Reduction Ratio**, depending on the operating frequency (50 Hz or 60 Hz).\n\n#### 1. 📉 4.3.17 CVGNE Reduction Ratio Data\n\nThe data shows reduction ratios for various belt speeds (listed in the first column).\n\n| Belt Speed (m/min) | Reduction Ratio (50 Hz) | Reduction Ratio (60 Hz) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **5** | 47.1 | 56.5 |\n| **7.5** | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| **9** | 26.2 | 31.4 |\n| **12.5** | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| **15** | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| **18** | 13.1 | 15.7 |\n| **21** | 11.3 | 13.1 |\n| **25** | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| **30** | 7.9 | 9.4 |\n| **35** | 6.5 | 7.9 |\n| **40** | 5.7 | 7.7 |\n| **50** | 3.9 | 4.7 |\n| **60** | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| **75** | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| **90** | 2.3 | 2.6 |\n| **100** | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| **120** | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| **150** | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n| **180** | 1.3 | 1.6 |\n\n#### 2. 📈 4.3.18 CVGRE Reduction Ratio Data\n\nThe data follows the same pattern but is specific to the 4.3.18 model.\n\n| Belt Speed (m/min) | Reduction Ratio (50 Hz) | Reduction Ratio (60 Hz) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **5** | 47.1 | 56.5 |\n| **7.5** | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| **9** | 26.2 | 31.4 |\n| **12.5** | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| **15** | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| **18** | 13.1 | 15.7 |\n| **21** | 11.3 | 13.1 |\n| **25** | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| **30** | 7.9 | 9.4 |\n| **35** | 6.5 | 7.9 |\n| **40** | 5.7 | 7.7 |\n| **50** | 3.9 | 4.7 |\n| **60** | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| **75** | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| **90** | 2.3 | 2.6 |\n| **100** | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| **120** | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| **150** | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n| **180** | 1.3 | 1.6 |\n\n***\n\n### Summary of Key Differences\n\nThe primary difference between the two models is the **Pulley Diameter**:\n\n*   **4.3.17 CVGNE:** Uses a smaller pulley ($\\varnothing 30$ mm).\n*   **4.3.18 CVGRE:** Uses a larger pulley ($\\varnothing 50$ mm).\n\nAll other functional specifications (Belt Width range, Power Range, and the corresponding performance tables) are identical for the specified operational speeds.\n\n[Page 25]\nThis page provides a detailed technical comparison and performance summary for two types of motorized conveyor/pulley systems: **4.3.19 CVGBE** and **4.3.20 CVGDE**. The information includes specifications, operational features, capacity charts, and performance tables.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ 4.3.19 CVGBE: Conveyor/Pulley System (Left Side)\n\n**Overall Description:** This system is designed for flat belt conveyance using a single belt and includes a dedicated head drive.\n\n### 🛠️ Special Features & Specifications\n*   **Conveyor Type:** Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Pulley Diameter ($\\emptyset$):** 30 mm.\n*   **Drive Mechanism:** Head drive.\n\n### 📐 Technical Data (Dimensions & Power)\n| Parameter | Range / Value | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 50–300 mm | |\n| **Length** | 190–2000 mm | |\n| **Weight** | 4.2–17.4 kg | |\n| **Voltage** | 220 V | |\n| **Frequency** | 50 Hz | |\n| **Power Output (W)** | Varies (Refer to table) | |\n\n### 📊 Conveyor Capacity Performance (Graph & Table)\nThis section graphs the relationship between Conveyor Capacity and Gearhead Reduction Ratio, tested at 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n**Key Data Trends:**\n*   The conveyor capacity remains relatively high across most reduction ratio values.\n*   Performance for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz is provided.\n\n**Performance Tables (Based on Gearhead Reduction Ratio):**\nThe table shows the expected performance capacity at different operational ratios.\n\n| Ratio | Conveyor Capacity (50 Hz) | Conveyor Capacity (60 Hz) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **1** | 5 | 4.7 |\n| **2** | 5.6 | 5.1 |\n| **3** | 7.5 | 6.4 |\n| **4** | 11.3 | 10.5 |\n| **6** | 18 | 17.8 |\n| **12** | 25 | 24 |\n| **20** | 35 | 34 |\n| **30** | 50 | 49 |\n\n*(Note: The graph visually confirms these proportional relationships.)*\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ 4.3.20 CVGDE: Conveyor/Pulley System (Right Side)\n\n**Overall Description:** This system is a variation of the CVGBE, featuring a larger pulley and different dimension ranges. It also includes a dedicated head drive.\n\n### 🛠️ Special Features & Specifications\n*   **Conveyor Type:** Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Pulley Diameter ($\\emptyset$):** 50 mm.\n*   **Drive Mechanism:** Head drive.\n\n### 📐 Technical Data (Dimensions & Power)\n| Parameter | Range / Value | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 50–300 mm | |\n| **Length** | 240–2000 mm | *(Slightly longer minimum length than CVGBE)* |\n| **Weight** | 6–25.7 kg | |\n| **Voltage** | 220 V | |\n| **Frequency** | 50 Hz | |\n| **Power Output (W)** | Varies (Refer to table) | |\n\n### 📊 Conveyor Capacity Performance (Graph & Table)\nThis section graphs the relationship between Conveyor Capacity and Gearhead Reduction Ratio, tested at 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n**Key Data Trends:**\n*   The performance curve is similar to CVGBE, indicating consistent operational capacity across the systems.\n*   Both 50 Hz and 60 Hz performance are provided.\n\n**Performance Tables (Based on Gearhead Reduction Ratio):**\nThe table shows the expected performance capacity at different operational ratios.\n\n| Ratio | Conveyor Capacity (50 Hz) | Conveyor Capacity (60 Hz) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **1** | 5 | 4.7 |\n| **2** | 5.6 | 5.1 |\n| **3** | 7.5 | 6.4 |\n| **4** | 11.3 | 10.5 |\n| **6** | 18 | 17.8 |\n| **12** | 25 | 24 |\n| **20** | 35 | 34 |\n| **30** | 50 | 49 |\n\n***\n\n## 📋 Summary Comparison & Key Data Points\n\n| Feature | 4.3.19 CVGBE | 4.3.20 CVGDE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Pulley Diameter** | 30 mm | 50 mm |\n| **Min. Length** | 190 mm | 240 mm |\n| **Min. Weight** | 4.2 kg | 6 kg |\n| **Belt Width Range** | 50–300 mm | 50–300 mm |\n| **Primary Function** | Conveying flat belts via head drive. | Conveying flat belts via head drive. |\n| **Operational Charts** | Capacity vs. Reduction Ratio (50/60 Hz) | Capacity vs. Reduction Ratio (50/60 Hz) |\n\n### General Technical Information\n*   **Product Category:** Conveyor Systems\n*   **Voltage:** 220 V\n*   **Frequency:** 50 Hz (The tables also provide 60 Hz data)\n*   **Applicable Fields:** Conveyor systems, general industrial machinery.\n\n### 🔗 Navigation/Footer\nThe page includes links for further information regarding:\n*   Connection\n*   Belt characteristics\n*   Accessories\n\n[Page 26]\nThis page provides a detailed technical summary and installation guide for Misumi conveyor systems, specifically models **4.3.21 CVGPE** and **4.3.22 CVGWE**. The content covers technical specifications, physical components, operational charts, and performance data.\n\n---\n\n## 🌐 Overview and General Specifications\n\n**Manufacturer:** Misumi\n**Topic:** Conveyor Systems - Installation and Operation\n**Application:** Conveying materials using flat belts and pulleys, driven by a central gearbox/motor unit.\n\n### 📐 Physical Setup (Diagrams)\nBoth models are depicted as linear conveyor assemblies. The diagrams illustrate a mechanism composed of:\n1.  A main structural frame.\n2.  Flat belts spanning the length.\n3.  Pulleys at both ends (driving and driven).\n4.  A centralized gearhead/motor unit responsible for power transfer.\n\n### ✨ Special Features (Shared)\nBoth models share the following operational features:\n*   Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   Pulley $\\text{Ø}$ 30 mm.\n*   Central drive.\n*   Belt with meandering prevention crosspiece.\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Technical Data & Model Comparison\n\nThe models are highly similar, differing slightly in their listed weight specifications.\n\n| Specification | 4.3.21 CVGPE (Left) | 4.3.22 CVGWE (Right) | Unit | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width (Min - Max)** | 50 - 300 | 50 - 300 | mm | |\n| **Length (Min - Max)** | 300 - 2000 | 300 - 2000 | mm | |\n| **Weight (Min - Max)** | 5.8 - 23.9 | 6 - 7.3 | kg | *Model 4.3.22 has a slightly higher minimum weight.* |\n| **Power Output (Min - Max)** | 6 - 25 | 6 - 25 | kW | |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | 230 | V | |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | 50 | Hz | |\n\n---\n\n## 📈 Performance and Capacity Data\n\nThe page includes two primary charts and two corresponding tables detailing the relationship between belt speed, conveyor capacity, and required gearhead reduction ratio.\n\n### 1. Conveyor Capacity Chart (Visual Data)\n*   **Y-Axis:** Conveyor Capacity (Implied metric of material handling rate).\n*   **X-Axis:** Belt Speed (Measured in m/min).\n*   **Relationship:** The chart shows that as the belt speed increases, the conveyor capacity increases linearly.\n\n### 2. Gearhead Reduction Ratio Chart (Visual Data)\n*   **Y-Axis:** Gearhead Reduction Ratio.\n*   **X-Axis:** Belt Speed (Measured in m/min).\n*   **Relationship:** The reduction ratio is stable across the operational range but decreases slightly as belt speed increases.\n\n### 📊 Detailed Performance Tables (Key Data)\n\nThese tables provide specific data points for Capacity and Reduction Ratio across various belt speeds (from 5 m/min to 150 m/min).\n\n#### A. Conveyor Capacity Data (Tonnage Capacity)\n\n| Belt Speed (m/min) | Capacity (50 Hz) | Capacity (60 Hz) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **5** | 47.1 | 56.5 |\n| **7.5** | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| **12** | 26.2 | 31.4 |\n| **15.5** | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| **18** | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| **25** | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| **30** | 7.9 | 9.4 |\n| **35** | 6.5 | 7.9 |\n| **50** | 4.7 | 5.7 |\n| **60** | 3.9 | 4.7 |\n| **75** | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| **90** | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| **100** | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| **120** | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| **150** | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n| **180** | 1.3 | 1.6 |\n\n***Key Observation:*** *Conveyor capacity is consistently higher when operated at 60 Hz compared to 50 Hz for all tested speeds.*\n\n#### B. Gearhead Reduction Ratio Data\n\n| Belt Speed (m/min) | Ratio (50 Hz) | Ratio (60 Hz) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **5** | 5.7 | 6.5 |\n| **7.5** | 3.4 | 3.7 |\n| **12** | 2.8 | 3.1 |\n| **15.5** | 2.2 | 2.6 |\n| **18** | 1.9 | 2.2 |\n| **25** | 1.5 | 1.8 |\n| **30** | 1.3 | 1.5 |\n| **35** | 1.1 | 1.3 |\n| **50** | 0.7 | 0.9 |\n| **60** | 0.5 | 0.7 |\n| **75** | 0.3 | 0.5 |\n| **90** | 0.2 | 0.6 |\n| **100** | 0.2 | 0.7 |\n| **120** | 0.1 | 0.8 |\n| **150** | 0.1 | 0.9 |\n| **180** | 0.1 | 1.1 |\n\n***Key Observation:*** *The required gearhead reduction ratio is generally lower at 60 Hz than at 50 Hz, especially at higher belt speeds.*\n\n---\n\n## 💾 Summary of Key Operational Principles\n\n1.  **Power Source:** The systems are designed for universal operation at 230V, 50/60 Hz.\n2.  **Operational Range:** The systems support belt speeds from 5 m/min up to 180 m/min.\n3.  **Performance Relationship:** Both Conveyor Capacity and Gearhead Reduction Ratio are functional metrics provided based on the operational frequency (50 Hz vs. 60 Hz).\n4.  **System Components:** The core system relies on a central drive unit, flat belts, and specialized pulleys for efficient, meandering-proof conveyance.\n\n[Page 27]\nThis document provides a detailed technical summary and operational overview for two high-power industrial conveyor systems: the **4.3.23 CVSSE** and the **4.3.24 CVSFE**. Both models are designed for demanding industrial applications.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ Overview of Conveyor Systems\n\nThe featured models are high-capacity, single-belt conveyor systems built for robust operation. The technical specifications for both models are highly similar, suggesting they serve comparable high-performance applications.\n\n### 🌟 Special Features (Shared)\n*   **Belt Type:** Flat belt\n*   **Belt Arrangement:** Single belt\n*   **Capacity:** High power\n\n***\n\n## 📄 Product Details: 4.3.23 CVSSE\n\n### 📊 Technical Specifications\n| Parameter | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | 100 – 500 | mm |\n| **Length** | 440 – 6000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 15.9 – 81.5 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 60 – 90 | kW |\n| **Voltage (V)** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### 📉 Operating Diagram: Belt Speed vs. Reduction Ratio\nThis diagram illustrates the operational range and the relationship between conveyor capacity and mechanical setup.\n\n*   **X-Axis:** Reduction Ratio (Input parameter).\n*   **Y-Axis:** Belt Speed (m/min).\n*   **Interpretation:** The capacity is shown changing based on whether the system operates at 50 Hz or 60 Hz. Generally, the capacity remains high across a wide operational range of reduction ratios.\n\n### 🗄️ Conveyor Capacity (Table)\nThe table provides specific capacity data points related to the operating frequency and reduction ratio.\n\n| Reduction Ratio | Capacity (50 Hz) | Capacity (60 Hz) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **7.5** | 56.4 | 67.7 |\n| **15** | 37.6 | 45.1 |\n| **22.5** | 22.6 | 27.1 |\n| **15** | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| **25** | 11.3 | 15.8 |\n| **30** | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| **45** | 7.8 | 9.4 |\n| **60** | 5.6 | 6.8 |\n| **7.5** | 4.7 | 5.6 |\n| **3** | 3.8 | 4.5 |\n| **100** | 2.8 | 3.4 |\n| **200** | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| **150** | 1.9 | 2.3 |\n| **180** | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n\n***\n\n## 📄 Product Details: 4.3.24 CVSFE\n\n### 📊 Technical Specifications\n*The technical specifications for the 4.3.24 CVSFE mirror those of the 4.3.23 CVSSE.*\n\n| Parameter | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | 100 – 500 | mm |\n| **Length** | 440 – 6000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 15.9 – 81.5 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 60 – 90 | kW |\n| **Voltage (V)** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### 📉 Operating Diagram: Belt Speed vs. Reduction Ratio\nThe diagram and capacity data for the 4.3.24 CVSFE are identical to those provided for the 4.3.23 CVSSE, confirming consistent performance characteristics across the operational range.\n\n***\n\n## 🔑 Key Data Summary and Takeaways\n\n### 1. Consistent Performance\nBoth models offer identical specifications and operational graphs, suggesting they are highly interchangeable regarding performance metrics.\n\n### 2. Operational Range\n*   **Voltage:** 230 V\n*   **Frequency:** 50 Hz (standard)\n*   **Power Output:** A high range of 60 kW to 90 kW.\n*   **Adaptability:** The systems are designed to handle significant variations in **Reduction Ratio** and **Belt Speed**.\n\n### 3. Capacity Comparison (50 Hz vs. 60 Hz)\nWhen comparing capacity data:\n*   **High-Frequency Advantage:** The system consistently shows a higher capacity when operating at **60 Hz** compared to 50 Hz, particularly evident at lower reduction ratios (e.g., at a reduction ratio of 7.5, capacity is 67.7 at 60 Hz vs. 56.4 at 50 Hz).\n*   **Low-End Stability:** Even at high reduction ratios (e.g., 180), the capacity remains stable and substantial, indicating robust torque and handling capabilities across the operating spectrum.\n\n[Page 28]\nThis page provides a detailed technical summary and performance data for two models of conveyor pulley systems: the **4.3.25 CVSXE** and the **4.3.26 CVSYE**. The system appears to be designed for high-power, single-belt conveyance applications.\n\n***\n\n## 📄 Summary Overview\n\nThe document details the specifications and operational curves for two interchangeable conveyor pulley units. These units are designed to handle medium conveying lengths and feature robust, flat belt single-belt high-power transfer capabilities.\n\n### ⚙️ Model Identification & Diagrams\n\n*   **Models:**\n    *   **4.3.25 CVSXE**\n    *   **4.3.26 CVSYE**\n*   **Diagrams:** Both models are shown with a cross-section diagram illustrating a standard conveyor setup featuring a pulley driven by a central drive mechanism and utilizing a flat belt.\n\n### ⚙️ Technical Specifications (Shared Data)\n\nThe following specifications apply to both featured models:\n\n*   **Special Features:** Flat belt, single belt, high power.\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\phi 30$ mm\n*   **Drive Mechanism:** Central drive\n*   **Conveying Length:** Medium conveying length\n\n***\n\n## 📊 Performance Data Tables\n\nThe page includes two comprehensive tables demonstrating the relationship between belt speed, gearhead reduction ratio, belt width, torque, and weight for both models.\n\n### 1. Model 4.3.25 CVSXE Performance Data\n\nThis table outlines operational ranges for different combinations of belt width (mm), desired belt speed (rpm), and the necessary gearhead reduction ratio.\n\n| Belt Width (mm) | Belt Speed (rpm) | Torque ($\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$) | Conveyor Capacity / Weight ($\\text{kg}$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 100 - 500 | 5 | 47.1 | 37.1 | 56.5 |\n| 100 - 500 | 10 | 7.5 | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| 100 - 500 | 20 | 12.5 | 26.2 | 31.4 |\n| 100 - 500 | 30 | 15.5 | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| 100 - 500 | 50 | 25 | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| 100 - 500 | 60 | 30 | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n\n*(Note: The table shows corresponding data pairs, likely for different operational scenarios or load conditions.)*\n\n### 2. Model 4.3.26 CVSYE Performance Data\n\nThis table follows the same structure, providing operational data for the 4.3.26 model.\n\n| Belt Width (mm) | Belt Speed (rpm) | Torque ($\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$) | Conveyor Capacity / Weight ($\\text{kg}$) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 100 - 500 | 5 | 47.1 | 37.1 | 56.5 |\n| 100 - 500 | 10 | 7.5 | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| 100 - 500 | 20 | 12.5 | 26.2 | 31.4 |\n| 100 - 500 | 30 | 15.5 | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| 100 - 500 | 50 | 25 | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| 100 - 500 | 60 | 30 | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n\n***\n\n## 🎯 Key Data Takeaways\n\n1.  **Performance Range:** The system is highly versatile, accommodating various operational demands ranging from low-power, low-speed applications (e.g., 5 rpm) to high-power, high-speed applications (e.g., 60 rpm).\n2.  **Relationship between Speed and Torque:** The data consistently shows that as the **Belt Speed (rpm)** increases, the required **Torque ($\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$)** generally increases, which is typical for belt drive systems handling increasing load capacity.\n3.  **Efficiency:** The tables provide specific numerical values for the required torque and weight/capacity at discrete speed points, allowing engineers to select the optimal motor and gearing system.\n\n***\n\n## 💡 Further Information (Navigation)\n\nThe page concludes with links to related technical documentation, directing users to more detailed information regarding:\n\n*   **Connection** (Further information on connection details)\n*   **Belt characteristics** (Technical data on belts)\n*   **Accessories** (Available complementary parts)\n\n[Page 29]\nThis page is a detailed technical datasheet for two models of full-belt conveyors: the **4.3.27 CVSFAE** and the **4.3.28 CVSFBE**. It provides specifications, operating diagrams, and performance curves illustrating the operational limits and capacities of the conveyor system.\n\n---\n\n## 📄 Overview of the Datasheet\n\n**Topic:** Full-Belt Conveyors (Misumi)\n**Models Covered:** 4.3.27 CVSFAE (Left) and 4.3.28 CVSFBE (Right)\n**Key Purpose:** To provide technical parameters, structural data, and performance graphs for selecting the correct conveyor system based on speed and load requirements.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ Product 1: 4.3.27 CVSFAE\n\n**(Image included: Diagram of the conveyor system)**\n\n### Special Features\n*   **Type:** Full-belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\emptyset$ 30 mm.\n*   **Drive:** Head drive.\n*   **Use:** Total surface area usable for transport.\n\n### 📐 Technical Data\n| Parameter | Specification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width (mm)** | 60–300 |\n| **Length (mm)** | 280–2000 |\n| **Weight (kg)** | 4–16.3 |\n| **Voltage (V)** | 230 |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 |\n\n### 📈 Performance Graphs and Tables\nThe section includes graphs detailing **Conveyor Capacity** and **Gearhead Reduction Ratio** relative to the belt speed (ranging from 0 to 30 m/min).\n\n#### 1. Conveyor Capacity (W)\n*   **Description:** Shows the maximum power/capacity the conveyor can handle at various speeds.\n*   **Data Interpretation:** Capacity is provided for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz operation. As speed increases, the capacity generally remains high and relatively stable across the operating range.\n\n#### 2. Gearhead Reduction Ratio\n*   **Description:** Shows the reduction ratio of the gearhead drive unit relative to the belt speed.\n*   **Data Interpretation:** This ratio changes significantly as the belt speed increases.\n\n***\n\n## 🚀 Product 2: 4.3.28 CVSFBE\n\n**(Image included: Diagram of the conveyor system)**\n\n### Special Features\n*   **Type:** Full-belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\emptyset$ 50 mm.\n*   **Drive:** Head drive.\n*   **Use:** Total surface area usable for transport.\n\n### 📐 Technical Data\n| Parameter | Specification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width (mm)** | 60–300 |\n| **Length (mm)** | 280–2000 |\n| **Weight (kg)** | 6–23.9 |\n| **Voltage (V)** | 230 |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 |\n\n### 📈 Performance Graphs and Tables\nThis section contains performance curves identical in function to Product 1, illustrating the operational characteristics for the larger pulley system.\n\n#### 1. Conveyor Capacity (W)\n*   **Data Interpretation:** Shows the operational capacity vs. speed.\n*   **Tables (Representative Data):**\n    *   **At 50 Hz:** Capacity remains strong across the speed range (e.g., near 150 m/min, capacity is around 18 W).\n    *   **At 60 Hz:** Capacity also remains high across the speed range.\n\n#### 2. Gearhead Reduction Ratio\n*   **Tables (Representative Data):**\n    *   **At 50 Hz:** The ratio starts around 1.5–1.6 at low speeds and decreases gradually as speed increases.\n    *   **At 60 Hz:** The ratio follows a similar downward trend, indicating the mechanical gearing adjustment needed for higher operational speeds.\n\n***\n\n## 🌟 Summary of Key Differences and Specifications\n\n| Feature | 4.3.27 CVSFAE (Left) | 4.3.28 CVSFBE (Right) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Pulley Diameter** | $\\emptyset$ 30 mm | $\\emptyset$ 50 mm |\n| **Weight Range (kg)** | 4–16.3 | 6–23.9 |\n| **Belt Width Range** | 60–300 mm | 60–300 mm |\n| **Voltage/Frequency** | 230V / 50 Hz | 230V / 50 Hz |\n| **Conveying Principle** | Full-belt, Single-belt | Full-belt, Single-belt |\n| **Key Difference** | Smaller pulley size, lighter weight. | Larger pulley size, heavier weight. |\n\n***\n\n## 🗂️ Further Information (Navigation)\nThe bottom section acts as a navigation guide, directing the user to corresponding pages for detailed information:\n\n*   **Connection:** Page 43\n*   **Belt Characteristics:** Page 36\n*   **Accessories:** Page 63\n\n[Page 30]\nThis page provides a detailed technical comparison and operational guide for two models of full-belt conveyors: **4.3.29 CVSFCE** and **4.3.30 CVSFDE**. The summary below integrates all key data, specifications, and diagrams presented.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Overview and Product Comparison\n\nThe page details two heavy-duty, full-belt conveyor systems designed for industrial installation and operation. Both models share general belt conveyor characteristics but differ in their specified pulley diameters.\n\n### **Key Product Specifications (Common)**\n*   **Type:** Full-belt conveyor, single belt.\n*   **Operation:** Includes Head drive.\n*   **Application:** Conveying materials (Capacity measured in tons).\n*   **Further Information Available On:** Connection, Belt characteristics, Accessories.\n\n| Parameter | Unit | Specification |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | mm | 70 – 300 |\n| **Length** | mm | 280 – 2000 |\n| **Weight** | kg | 4 – 16.3 (4.3.29) / 6 – 23.9 (4.3.30) |\n| **Power (W)** | W | 230 |\n| **Frequency** | Hz | 50 |\n\n### **Model Differences (Key Feature)**\n\n| Model | Pulley Diameter | Beltway Feature |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **4.3.29 CVSFCE** | $\\emptyset 30 \\text{ mm}$ | Belt with meandering prevention crosspiece |\n| **4.3.30 CVSFDE** | $\\emptyset 50 \\text{ mm}$ | Belt with meandering prevention crosspiece |\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Technical Data Tables (Capacity)\n\nThe tables illustrate the conveyor's carrying capacity (in tons) based on different belt speeds (m/s) and the operating frequency (50 Hz vs. 60 Hz).\n\n### **1. Conveyor Capacity for Model 4.3.29 CVSFCE**\n\n| Belt Speed (m/s) | Capacity (ton) @ 50 Hz | Capacity (ton) @ 60 Hz |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 5 | 5.6 | 6.7 |\n| 7.5 | 37.6 | 45.1 |\n| 12 | 22.6 | 37.1 |\n| 15 | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| 20 | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| 25 | 11.3 | 13.5 |\n| 30 | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| 35 | 6.8 | 9.4 |\n| 40 | 5.6 | 6.8 |\n| 50 | 4.7 | 5.6 |\n| 60 | 3.8 | 4.7 |\n| 75 | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| 100 | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| 120 | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| 150 | 2.2 | 2.4 |\n| 180 | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n\n### **2. Conveyor Capacity for Model 4.3.30 CVSFDE**\n\n| Belt Speed (m/s) | Capacity (ton) @ 50 Hz | Capacity (ton) @ 60 Hz |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 5 | 37.1 | 56.5 |\n| 7.5 | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| 12 | 26.2 | 31.4 |\n| 15 | 18.8 | 22.6 |\n| 20 | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| 25 | 11.3 | 13.5 |\n| 30 | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| 35 | 6.8 | 9.4 |\n| 40 | 5.6 | 6.8 |\n| 50 | 4.7 | 5.6 |\n| 60 | 3.8 | 4.7 |\n| 75 | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| 100 | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| 120 | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| 150 | 2.2 | 2.4 |\n| 180 | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n\n---\n\n## 📈 Operational Diagrams (Graphs)\n\nBoth models are accompanied by a graph illustrating the relationship between **Conveyor Capacity**, **Belt Speed**, and **Gearhead Reduction Ratio**.\n\n**Diagram Analysis:**\n*   The graphs show two distinct performance curves (one for 50 Hz and one for 60 Hz).\n*   **X-axis:** Gearhead reduction ratio (R/N).\n*   **Y-axis:** Conveyor capacity (ton).\n*   The curves demonstrate that for a given capacity, the capacity increases as the ratio increases (moving from left to right on the graph). The 60 Hz performance is generally shown to be higher or equal to the 50 Hz performance for the same ratio, confirming the data presented in the table section.\n\n*(Note: The graph itself is graphical representation of the data, not a standalone table.)*\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Summary of Key Operating Principles\n\n1.  **Performance Scaling:** Both models are designed for robust performance, with capacity being a function of the belt speed and the gearhead reduction ratio.\n2.  **Pulley Impact:** The difference in pulley size ($\\emptyset 30 \\text{ mm}$ vs. $\\emptyset 50 \\text{ mm}$) likely influences the overall mechanical design and weight, though the basic power (230 W) and frequency (50 Hz) remain constant.\n3.  **Data Consistency:** The capacity data provided in the detailed tables mirrors the trends shown in the graphs and confirms the operational range of the systems.\n4.  **Low Speed Operation:** At low belt speeds (e.g., $5 \\text{ m/s}$), the capacity is highest, especially for the 4.3.30 CVSFDE model (up to 56.5 tons @ 60 Hz).\n5.  **High Speed Limitation:** As belt speed increases, the maximum achievable capacity decreases across all models.\n\n[Page 31]\nThis page provides detailed technical specifications, diagrams, and operating data for two models of flat belt conveyors: the **4.3.31 CVSJAE** and the **4.3.32 CVSMAE**.\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Detailed Summary of Conveyor Models\n\n### ⚙️ 1. Product: 4.3.31 CVSJAE (Conveyor System)\n\n**Diagram:** The page includes a detailed technical diagram of the conveyor unit.\n\n#### Key Features and Technical Data\n*   **Special Features:**\n    *   Flat belt conveyors, single belt.\n    *   Pulley $\\emptyset$ 30 mm.\n    *   Central drive.\n    *   Belt with meandering prevention crosspiece.\n*   **Technical Data:**\n    *   **Bolt width (mm):** 50–300\n    *   **Length (mm):** 220–800\n    *   **Weight (kg):** 6.7–14.3\n    *   **Power output (W):** 230\n    *   **Voltage (V):** 230\n    *   **Frequency (Hz):** 50\n\n#### Conveyer Capacity Graph\nThe page features a **Conveyer Capacity** graph illustrating the relationship between load (capacity) and belt speed. The graph shows a clear inverse correlation: as the belt speed increases, the usable conveyor capacity (load) decreases.\n\n#### Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Performance Table)\nThis table details the operational reduction ratios for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz frequencies.\n\n| Speed (mm/min) | 50 Hz Ratio | 60 Hz Ratio |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 5 | 47.1 | 56.5 |\n| 7.5 | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| 12.5 | 26.2 | 31.4 |\n| 18 | 22.8 | 28 |\n| 15 | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| 18 | 13.1 | 15.7 |\n| 25 | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| 30 | 7.9 | 9.4 |\n| 35 | 6.5 | 7.9 |\n| 50 | 5.7 | 9.7 |\n| 60 | 3.9 | 7.1 |\n| 75 | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| 90 | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| 100 | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| 120 | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| 150 | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n| 180 | 1.3 | 1.6 |\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 2. Product: 4.3.32 CVSMAE (Short Design Conveyor)\n\n**Diagram:** The page includes a detailed technical diagram of the conveyor unit, noting its "short design."\n\n#### Key Features and Technical Data\n*   **Special Features:**\n    *   Flat belt conveyors, single belt, short design.\n    *   Pulley $\\emptyset$ 70 mm.\n    *   Integrated drive.\n    *   Reduced conveyor height.\n*   **Technical Data:**\n    *   **Bolt width (mm):** 60–150\n    *   **Length (mm):** 415–2000\n    *   **Weight (kg):** 6.2–18.7\n    *   **Power output (W):** 230\n    *   **Voltage (V):** 230\n    *   **Frequency (Hz):** 50\n\n#### Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Performance Table)\nThis table provides the operational reduction ratios for the CVSMAE model, mirroring the structure of the first model.\n\n| Speed (mm/min) | 50 Hz Ratio | 60 Hz Ratio |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 5 | 15 | 22.0 |\n| 7.5 | 18 | 22.0 |\n| 12.5 | 15.2 | 15.8 |\n| 18 | 11.0 | 13.2 |\n| 25 | 9.4 | 11.0 |\n| 30 | 7.9 | 9.4 |\n| 35 | 6.5 | 7.9 |\n| 50 | 5.7 | 9.7 |\n| 60 | 3.9 | 7.1 |\n| 75 | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| 90 | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| 100 | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| 120 | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| 150 | 1.6 | 1.9 |\n| 180 | 1.3 | 1.6 |\n\n---\n\n## ℹ️ Further Information and Navigation\n\nThe bottom section of the page indicates that comprehensive support and additional specifications are available for the following topics:\n\n*   **Connection:** (See page 43)\n*   **Belt characteristics:** (See page 36)\n*   **Accessories:** (See page 63)\n\n[Page 32]\nThis page provides detailed technical specifications, features, and operational data for two different models of conveyor systems: **4.3.33 CVLPAE** and **4.3.34 CVMAE**. Both models utilize flat belt conveyors but differ significantly in their pulley size, drive mechanism, and available technical ranges.\n\nHere is a detailed summary, including tables, diagrams, and key data.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Product Summary\n\n### 1. 4.3.33 CVLPAE (Conveyor System)\n\nThis model features a compact, central drive system suitable for specific applications.\n\n**🏷️ Special Features:**\n*   Flat belt conveyors, single belt\n*   Pulley $\\text{D} \\text{ } 15 \\text{ mm}$\n*   **Central drive**\n*   Low design\n\n**📊 Technical Data (Specifications):**\n\n| Specification | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | $60 \\sim 300$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| **Length** | $360 \\sim 2000$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| **Power Output** | $25$ | $\\text{W}$ |\n| **Voltage** | $230$ | $\\text{V}$ |\n| **Frequency** | $50$ | $\\text{Hz}$ |\n\n---\n\n### 2. 4.3.34 CVMAE (Conveyor System)\n\nThis model offers greater flexibility with a larger pulley and a head drive mechanism.\n\n**🏷️ Special Features:**\n*   Flat belt conveyors, single belt\n*   Pulley $\\text{D} \\text{ } 30 \\text{ mm}$\n*   **Head drive**\n*   Selectable motor position\n\n**📊 Technical Data (Specifications):**\n\n| Specification | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | $50 \\sim 300$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| **Length** | $200 \\sim 2000$ | $\\text{mm}$ |\n| **Power Output** | $25$ | $\\text{W}$ |\n| **Voltage** | $230$ | $\\text{V}$ |\n| **Frequency** | $50$ | $\\text{Hz}$ |\n\n---\n\n## 📈 Performance Charts & Data Analysis\n\nBoth models include two primary technical graphs and a reduction ratio table used for operational planning.\n\n### A. Conveyor Capacity Diagram (Diagram)\n\nThis diagram illustrates the relationship between **Conveyor Power** and operational speed/load, helping users determine the maximum effective capacity of the unit at various speeds.\n\n*   **Axes:** The Y-axis represents **Conveyor Power** (capacity) and the X-axis represents speed/load (indicated by the numerical scale).\n*   **Function:** The curved line shows how power requirements relate to operational parameters, allowing the user to select the appropriate speed/load combination for continuous operation.\n\n### B. Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Table)\n\nThis table defines the relationship between the input speed/power and the resulting output speed/power, which is critical for mechanical integration.\n\n#### 1. 4.3.33 CVLPAE Reduction Ratio (Table)\n\n| Input Speed (RPM) | Output Speed (RPM) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| 5 | 37.1 |\n| 10 | 31.4 |\n| 15 | 26.2 |\n| 20 | 21.5 |\n| 25 | 18.8 |\n| 30 | 16.7 |\n| 35 | 15.7 |\n| 40 | 14.4 |\n| 50 | 12.8 |\n| 60 | 11.1 |\n\n#### 2. 4.3.34 CVMAE Reduction Ratio (Table)\n\n| Input Speed (RPM) | Output Speed (RPM) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| 5 | 37.7 |\n| 10 | 31.6 |\n| 15 | 26.4 |\n| 20 | 21.7 |\n| 25 | 18.8 |\n| 30 | 16.7 |\n| 35 | 15.7 |\n| 40 | 14.4 |\n| 50 | 12.8 |\n| 60 | 11.1 |\n\n*(Note: The reduction ratios are highly similar for both models, suggesting standardized operational scaling, though the CVMAE appears to have slightly higher initial output values.)*\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Key Comparative Data Summary\n\nThe most significant differences between the two models are highlighted below, as they dictate the system's installation and function.\n\n| Feature | 4.3.33 CVLPAE | 4.3.34 CVMAE | Key Difference |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Pulley Diameter ($\\text{D}$)** | $15 \\text{ mm}$ | $30 \\text{ mm}$ | Larger pulley for CVMAE (more torque/force application). |\n| **Drive System** | Central drive | Head drive | Determines the motor's location and system layout. |\n| **Bolt Width Range** | $60 \\sim 300 \\text{ mm}$ | $50 \\sim 300 \\text{ mm}$ | CVMAE has a slightly narrower minimum width range. |\n| **Overall Design** | Low design | Standard/Head drive design | Affects installation height and footprint. |\n| **Power/Voltage** | $25 \\text{ W} / 230 \\text{ V}$ | $25 \\text{ W} / 230 \\text{ V}$ | Identical core electrical specifications. |\n\n[Page 33]\nThis page provides a detailed comparison and specification guide for two types of conveyor systems: the **4.3.35 CVMBE** and the **4.3.36 CVSTCE**.\n\nBelow is a detailed summary, including key data, specifications, and interpretations of the graphs and tables.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Product 1: 4.3.35 CVMBE (Belt Conveyor)\n\nThis system appears to be a standard, belt-driven conveyor (likely designed for smooth, continuous transfer).\n\n### 🖼️ Diagram & Key Features\n*   **Visual:** A diagram of a standard conveyor belt running over rollers.\n*   **Special Features:**\n    *   Flat belt, single belt.\n    *   Pulley diameter ($\\text{\\O}$): $30 \\text{ mm}$.\n    *   Drive mechanism: Head drive.\n\n### 📋 Technical Data\n| Specification | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | $50 - 300$ | mm |\n| **Length** | $200 - 2000$ | mm |\n| **Weight** | $10 - 30$ | kg |\n| **Power Output** | $25 - 200$ | kW |\n| **Voltage** | $230$ | V |\n| **Frequency** | $50$ | Hz |\n\n### 📊 Performance Data (Torque vs. Speed)\nThe top graph illustrates the **Conveyor Capacity** (Torque $\\text{kW}\\cdot\\text{m}$) in relation to speed (Hz). The capacity peaks at approximately $10-15 \\text{ kW}\\cdot\\text{m}$ around 20-30 Hz.\n\n#### Detailed Torque/Speed Table (Key Operational Data)\nThis table provides the maximum obtainable torque at various operating loads for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n| Load (Tons) | Torque @ 50 Hz ($\\text{kW}\\cdot\\text{m}$) | Torque @ 60 Hz ($\\text{kW}\\cdot\\text{m}$) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **7.5** | $56.4$ | $67.7$ |\n| **15** | $37.6$ | $45.1$ |\n| **22.5** | $22.6$ | $27.1$ |\n| **30** | $18.5$ | $22.6$ |\n| **36** | $11.3$ | $13.5$ |\n| **50** | $9.4$ | $11.3$ |\n| **75** | $6.0$ | $8.4$ |\n| **100** | $4.7$ | $5.6$ |\n| **150** | $3.8$ | $4.5$ |\n| **200** | $2.4$ | $2.8$ |\n| **300** | $1.6$ | $1.9$ |\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ Product 2: 4.3.36 CVSTCE (Timing Belt Conveyor)\n\nThis system is designed with a timing belt, suggesting high synchronization and controlled movement, making it ideal for material that requires precise handling.\n\n### 🖼️ Diagram & Key Features\n*   **Visual:** A diagram of a conveyor system with a more robust, enclosed structure, utilizing a timing belt.\n*   **Special Features:**\n    *   Timing belt, single belt.\n    *   Pulley diameter ($\\text{\\O}$): $19, 20 \\text{ mm}$.\n    *   Drive mechanism: Head drive.\n\n### 📋 Technical Data\n| Specification | Range/Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | $10 - 20$ | mm |\n| **Length** | $245 - 2000$ | mm |\n| **Weight** | $3 - 7$ | kg |\n| **Power Output** | $6 - 20$ | kW |\n| **Voltage** | $230$ | V |\n| **Frequency** | $50$ | Hz |\n\n### 📊 Performance Data (Torque/Speed)\nThis system features a dedicated table for operational data, listing the maximum torque at various load levels for 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n#### Detailed Torque/Speed Table (Key Operational Data)\n| Load (Tons) | Torque @ 50 Hz ($\\text{kW}\\cdot\\text{m}$) | Torque @ 60 Hz ($\\text{kW}\\cdot\\text{m}$) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **5** | $12.5$ | $14.4$ |\n| **10** | $15.0$ | $18.0$ |\n| **15** | $18.0$ | $20.0$ |\n| **25** | $30.0$ | $36.0$ |\n| **30** | $42.0$ | $50.0$ |\n| **50** | $60.0$ | $72.0$ |\n| **75** | $80.0$ | $96.0$ |\n| **100** | $100.0$ | $120.0$ |\n| **150** | $130.0$ | $150.0$ |\n| **180** | $160.0$ | $180.0$ |\n\n***\n\n## ℹ️ Summary and Related Information\n\nThe page concludes with standard navigational elements directing the user to related detailed documentation:\n\n*   **Connection/Belt:** From page 43\n*   **Belt characteristics:** From page 36\n*   **Accessories:** From page 63\n\n---\n### **🚀 Quick Comparison Overview**\n\n| Feature | 4.3.35 CVMBE | 4.3.36 CVSTCE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Primary Belt Type** | Flat belt | Timing belt |\n| **Ideal Use Case** | General continuous material movement | Precise, synchronized material handling |\n| **Pulley Diameter** | $\\text{\\O} 30 \\text{ mm}$ | $\\text{\\O} 19, 20 \\text{ mm}$ |\n| **Weight Range** | $10 - 30 \\text{ kg}$ (Heavier duty) | $3 - 7 \\text{ kg}$ (Lighter duty) |\n| **Power Output Range**| $25 - 200 \\text{ kW}$ | $6 - 20 \\text{ kW}$ |\n\n[Page 34]\nThis document provides detailed technical specifications and operating instructions for two types of conveyor systems: the **4.3.37 CVSTRE** and the **4.3.38 CVGTAE**.\n\nThe summary is broken down by model, followed by general technical data and cross-references.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ 1. 4.3.37 CVSTRE System (Center Drive)\n\nThis system features a central motor setup and is designed for space-efficient operation.\n\n### **📋 Special Features**\n*   **Belt:** Timing belt, single belt setup.\n*   **Pulley:** Diameter of 19 to 20 mm.\n*   **Drive:** Center drive.\n*   **Design:** Space-saving design.\n\n### **📊 Technical Data**\n| Parameter | Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 10, 20 | mm |\n| **Length** | 330–2000 | mm |\n| **Power (W)** | 3–9.6 | kW |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### **📈 Conveyor Capacity vs. Reduction Ratio**\nThe diagram illustrates the operational capacity (measured in units of load/power) as a function of the reduction ratio.\n\n**Key Data Trend:** Capacity is highest at low reduction ratios and drops significantly as the ratio increases.\n\n#### **Operational Capacity Table (Load/Power)**\n| Reduction Ratio | 60 Hz (Max Load) | 50 Hz (Max Load) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1.0** | 10 | 10 |\n| **2.0** | 12.5 | 12.0 |\n| **5.0** | 15 | 14.4 |\n| **10.0** | 20 | 18 |\n| **25.0** | 30 | 28 |\n| **50.0** | 60 | 56 |\n| **100.0** | 150 | 140 |\n| **200.0** | 300 | 280 |\n*(Note: The graph suggests capacity scales linearly with the reduction ratio up to a certain point, after which the drop-off is exponential.)*\n\n***\n\n## 🚀 2. 4.3.38 CVGTAE System (Head Drive)\n\nThis system uses a head drive mechanism and includes stoppers for controlled operation.\n\n### **📋 Special Features**\n*   **Belt:** Timing belt, double track setup.\n*   **Pulley:** Diameter of 30 mm.\n*   **Drive:** Head drive.\n*   **Safety:** Stoppers can be installed in the gap.\n\n### **📊 Technical Data**\n| Parameter | Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 20, 30 | mm |\n| **Length** | 255–3000 | mm |\n| **Power (W)** | 6–10.6 | kW |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### **📈 Conveyor Capacity vs. Reduction Ratio**\nThe capacity is highly dependent on the reduction ratio.\n\n**Key Data Trend:** Similar to the 4.3.37 model, capacity declines significantly as the reduction ratio increases.\n\n#### **Operational Capacity Table (Load/Power)**\n| Reduction Ratio | 60 Hz (Max Load) | 50 Hz (Max Load) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1.0** | 5 | 5 |\n| **2.0** | 6.0 | 5.0 |\n| **5.0** | 12.5 | 10.4 |\n| **10.0** | 20 | 18 |\n| **25.0** | 30 | 26 |\n| **50.0** | 60 | 56 |\n| **100.0** | 150 | 140 |\n| **200.0** | 300 | 280 |\n\n***\n\n## 📄 3. General Specifications and Operation Notes\n\n### **Technical Details Comparison**\n| Feature | 4.3.37 CVSTRE | 4.3.38 CVGTAE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Drive Type** | Center Drive (Space-saving) | Head Drive |\n| **Pulley Dia.** | 19–20 mm | 30 mm |\n| **Belt Width Range** | 10–20 mm | 20–30 mm |\n| **Capacity Dependency** | Reduces drastically with higher reduction ratios. | Reduces drastically with higher reduction ratios. |\n\n### **Operating Notes**\n*   **Power/Capacity:** The capacity charts show that the maximum load/power is achievable at the lowest reduction ratios and drops off dramatically as the ratio increases.\n*   **Frequency Dependence:** Performance metrics (shown in the tables) are provided for both 60 Hz and 50 Hz operations.\n*   **Motor Type:** The unit specifications are based on a standard 230V input.\n\n### **Further Information (Cross-Reference)**\nThe page concludes with links to related documentation:\n*   Connection (from page 43)\n*   Belt Characteristics (from page 36)\n*   Accessories (from page 63)\n\n[Page 35]\nThis page provides a detailed technical summary and product comparison for two models of industrial timing belt conveyors: **4.3.39 CVGTBE** and **4.3.40 CVGTNE**.\n\nThe summary below includes a comprehensive overview, technical specifications in tables, and an analysis of the operational data graphs.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Overview: CVG Timing Belt Conveyors\n\nThese products are industrial timing belt systems designed for conveyors, featuring a double track structure. They are utilized in machinery requiring precise belt movement and robust operational capacity.\n\n### 📝 Technical Data Comparison\n\n| Feature | 4.3.39 CVGTBE (Left) | 4.3.40 CVGTNE (Right) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Product Type** | Timing belt, conveyors, double track | Timing belt, conveyors, double track |\n| **Belt Width** | 80–300 mm | 80–300 mm |\n| **Length** | 265–3000 mm | 265–3000 mm |\n| **Weight (kg)** | 9.1–24.3 kg | 6.6–13.4 kg |\n| **Power Output (W)** | 25–220 W | 25–120 W |\n| **Voltage (V)** | 220 V | 230 V |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 Hz | 50 Hz |\n| **Installation Notes**| Stoppers, sensors can be installed in the gap. | Stoppers, sensors can be installed in the gap. |\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Detailed Product Specifications\n\n### 1. Model 4.3.39 CVGTBE (Left Side)\n\n**Technical Specifications:**\n\n*   **Belt Type:** Timing belt, conveyors, double track.\n*   **Measurement Range:**\n    *   Belt Width: 80–300 mm\n    *   Length: 265–3000 mm\n*   **Power/Weight:**\n    *   Weight: 9.1–24.3 kg\n    *   Power Output: 25–220 W\n*   **Electrical:**\n    *   Voltage: 220 V\n    *   Frequency: 50 Hz\n*   **Features:** Supports the installation of stoppers and sensors in the gap.\n\n**Operational Graph Data (Conveyor Capacity vs. Belt Speed):**\nThis graph details the maximum conveyor capacity (kg/m) achievable at different belt speeds and frequencies.\n\n| Frequency | Belt Speed (m/min) | Capacity (kg/m) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **50 Hz** | 30 | 20 |\n| **60 Hz** | 48 | 35 |\n\n--