atio vs. Belt Speed. | Capacity is quantified by Gearhead reduction ratio vs. Belt Speed. |\n\n### General Information\n\n*   **Connection/Belt Characteristics:** Detailed technical information is available (referencing pages 43 and 36).\n*   **Accessories:** Further details on accessories are available (referencing pages 43, 36, and 63).\n\n[Page 37]\nThis page provides detailed technical specifications and performance data for two models of electric belt conveyors: the **4.3.43 CVSSAE** and the **4.3.44 CVDSAE**. Both systems are designed for material handling and utilize a head drive system.\n\nHere is a detailed summary, including tables, descriptions of diagrams, and key data points.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ Model Comparison Overview\n\n| Feature | 4.3.43 CVSSAE | 4.3.44 CVDSAE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Type** | Stainless steel belt conveyors, single belt. | Flat belt conveyor with studs, single belt. |\n| **Pulleys** | $\\emptyset$ 50 mm | $\\emptyset$ 50 mm |\n| **Key Application Note** | General conveyor use (focus on stainless steel). | Suitable for foodstuffs, sloped design (focus on sanitary/studs). |\n| **Width Range** | Narrower (40–150 mm) | Wider (50–300 mm) |\n| **Length Range** | 250–2000 mm | 500–3000 mm |\n\n***\n\n## 📝 1. 4.3.43 CVSSAE (Stainless Steel Conveyor)\n\nThis model is specialized for use with stainless steel belts, suggesting applications requiring corrosion resistance or sanitation.\n\n### Specialized Features\n*   **Belting:** Stainless steel belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Head Drive:** Equipped with a dedicated head drive system.\n*   **Visual Diagram:** Illustrates the basic structure of a powered conveyor belt system.\n\n### Technical Data Table\n| Specification | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 40–150 | mm |\n| **Length** | 250–2000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 6–20 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 6–25 | W |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### Performance Graph (Gearhead Reduction Ratio)\nThe graph shows the relationship between **Belt Speed (mm/s)** and **Gearhead Reduction Ratio**.\n*   **Visualization:** The plot features two lines (labeled 50 Hz/150 and 50 Hz/150), demonstrating that as the belt speed increases, the required gearhead reduction ratio decreases.\n*   **Key Data Points (Ratio vs. Speed):**\n    *   At a speed of 5 mm/s, the ratio is approximately 20.\n    *   At a speed of 15 mm/s, the ratio is approximately 12.\n    *   At a speed of 25 mm/s, the ratio is approximately 8.\n\n***\n\n## 🔩 2. 4.3.44 CVDSAE (Flat Belt Conveyor)\n\nThis model is optimized for industrial settings, particularly those involving foodstuffs or slopes, due to its flat belt and stud design.\n\n### Specialized Features\n*   **Belting:** Flat belt conveyor with studs, single belt.\n*   **Suitable For:** Foodstuffs and sloped designs.\n*   **Head Drive:** Equipped with a dedicated head drive system.\n*   **Visual Diagram:** Illustrates the structured conveyor belt system.\n\n### Technical Data Table\n| Specification | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 50–300 | mm |\n| **Length** | 500–3000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 11–37.6 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 20–100 | W |\n| **Voltage** | 230 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### Performance Graph (Gearhead Reduction Ratio)\nThe graph tracks the relationship between **Belt Speed (mm/s)** and **Gearhead Reduction Ratio**.\n*   **Visualization:** The plot shows a similar inverse relationship; as belt speed increases, the required reduction ratio decreases.\n*   **Key Data Points (Ratio vs. Speed):**\n    *   At a speed of 5 mm/s, the ratio is approximately 25.\n    *   At a speed of 15 mm/s, the ratio is approximately 15.\n    *   At a speed of 25 mm/s, the ratio is approximately 8.\n\n***\n\n## 🌐 Key Universal Information\n\n**Common Specifications:**\n*   **Voltage:** 230 V\n*   **Frequency:** 50 Hz\n\n**Further Information:**\nThe page notes that detailed information regarding the belt characteristics and accessories for both product lines can be found in the following sections (page numbers):\n*   Belt characteristics: Pages 36, 63\n*   Accessories: Pages 43, 36, 63\n\n[Page 38]\nThis page is a technical catalog listing two different models of conveyor or belt systems (4.3.45 CVDSBE and 4.3.46 CVSPCE) from MISUMI, detailing their features, technical specifications, operational curves, and performance data.\n\nHere is a detailed summary:\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ I. Product 1: 4.3.45 CVDSBE (Belt System)\n\nThis model utilizes a flat belt mechanism.\n\n### 🟢 Key Data and Specifications\n| Parameter | Specification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Special Features** | Flat belt with studs, single belt. |\n| **Bolt Width** | 50–300 mm |\n| **Length** | 500–3000 mm |\n| **Weight (kg)** | 11–37.8 |\n| **Power Output (W)** | 230 |\n| **Voltage (V)** | 220 |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 |\n\n### 📊 Performance Diagram: Gearhead Reduction Ratio\nThe graph illustrates the relationship between **Load (kg)** and the **Gearhead reduction ratio**. This shows how the system's operational speed changes relative to the applied load.\n\n*(The diagram features a bell curve shape, typically showing maximum efficiency or operational range at a specific intermediate load/ratio.)*\n\n### ⚙️ Table: Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Speed vs. Load)\n\nThe ratio data is provided for two different standard frequencies: 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n#### A. 50 Hz Reduction Data\n| Load (kg) | Speed (RPM) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| 7.5 | 31.4 |\n| 12.5 | 28.6 |\n| 15 | 25.8 |\n| 18 | 22.8 |\n| 21.5 | 19.7 |\n| 25 | 17.9 |\n| 30 | 15.7 |\n| 36 | 13.1 |\n| 50 | 9.4 |\n| 75 | 5.7 |\n\n#### B. 60 Hz Reduction Data\n| Load (kg) | Speed (RPM) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| 7.5 | 31.4 |\n| 12.5 | 28.6 |\n| 15 | 25.8 |\n| 18 | 22.8 |\n| 21.5 | 19.7 |\n| 25 | 17.9 |\n| 30 | 15.7 |\n| 36 | 13.1 |\n| 50 | 9.4 |\n| 75 | 5.7 |\n\n***\n\n## 🔩 II. Product 2: 4.3.46 CVSPCE (Chain Belt System)\n\nThis model utilizes a plastic