le the core technical specifications are nearly identical, the primary difference lies in their specialized features.\n\n| Feature | 4.3.23 CVSCE | 4.3.24 CVSFE |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Special Features** | Flat belt conveyors, single belt, high power. | Flat belt conveyors, single belt, high power. |\n| **Pulley Size** | Ø 30, 60 mm | Ø 30, 60 mm |\n| **Drive** | Head drive | Head drive |\n| **Key Feature** | **Medium conveying length** | **Belt with meandering prevention crosspiece** |\n\n## 📏 Shared Technical Data (Common to both 4.3.23 and 4.3.24)\n\nThe operational ranges and electrical specifications are consistent for both conveyor systems.\n\n### ⚙️ Technical Specifications\n*   **Belt Width (W):** 100 mm to 500 mm\n*   **Length (L):** 440 mm to 6000 mm\n*   **Power (P):** 15.9 kW to 81.5 kW\n*   **Voltage (V):** 230 V\n*   **Frequency (Hz):** 50 Hz (Note: Performance data is provided for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz operation.)\n\n## 📈 Performance and Capacity Data\n\nThe page includes three identical performance graphs/tables for each model, detailing **Conveyor Capacity** (measured in units/min) based on operational variables.\n\n### A. Diagrammatic Representation (Capacity Graphs)\nBoth models feature three graphs (labeled 1, 2, and 3) illustrating how conveyor capacity changes based on a combination of motor power, belt width, and speed/belt operation.\n\n*   **Axes:** The capacity (Y-axis) is measured in units/min.\n*   **Variability:** The curves demonstrate that capacity is heavily dependent on both the operational frequency (50 Hz vs. 60 Hz) and the selected operational parameters (power/width).\n*   **Key Trend:** The capacity generally increases when operating at 60 Hz compared to 50 Hz.\n\n### B. Capacity Tables (Key Data Points)\nThe tables provide specific capacity readings for various conditions, highlighting the frequency difference.\n\n| Operational Setting | 50 Hz Capacity (Units/min) | 60 Hz Capacity (Units/min) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Low Power/Width** | 5.7 | 6.4 |\n| **Medium Power/Width** | 9.1 | 12.2 |\n| **High Power/Width** | 13.3 | 16.8 |\n| **Maximum Capacity** | 18.0 | 24.0 |\n\n*(Note: The specific capacity numbers displayed in the small tables are replicated for both 4.3.23 and 4.3.24, indicating comparable performance.)*\n\n## 📚 Footer and Further Information\n\nThe bottom section provides navigational links for further research on the product line:\n\n| Section | From Page | Section | From Page |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belting** | $\\blacktriangledown$ from page 43 | **Belting Characteristics** | $\\blacktriangledown$ from page 36 |\n| **Connection** | $\\blacktriangledown$ from page 43 | **Accessories** | $\\blacktriangledown$ from page 63 |\n| **Belting Characteristics** | $\\blacktriangledown$ from page 36 | | |\n\n[Page 28]\nThis page provides detailed technical specifications and operational data for two models of conveyor pulley systems: the **4.3.25 CVSXE** and the **4.3.26 CVSYE**. The overall system is designed for high-power, single-belt conveying applications.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ General System Overview\n\n**Product Category:** Conveyor Systems / Pulley Drive\n**Common Features (Applies to both models):**\n*   **Conveying Type:** Flat belt conveyors, single belt, high power.\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $30 \\text{ mm}$.\n*   **Drive Mechanism:** Central drive.\n*   **Application:** Medium conveying length.\n*   **Diagram:** The diagrams illustrate the pulley assembly connected to a conveyor belt system.\n\n***\n\n## 📑 Technical Specifications (Shared Data)\n\n| Parameter | Unit | Range |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | $\\text{mm}$ | $100 - 500$ |\n| **Length** | $\\text{mm}$ | $480 - 6000$ |\n| **Weight** | $\\text{kg}$ | $20 - 94$ |\n| **Power output** | $\\text{W}$ | $60 - 90$ |\n| **Voltage** | $\\text{V}$ | $220$ |\n| **Frequency** | $\\text{Hz}$ | $50$ |\n\n**Note:** Specifications are dependent on the design of the conveyor.\n\n***\n\n## 📊 Performance and Torque Data\n\nThe provided tables detail the required torque and power output (in $\\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}$ and $\\text{W}$, respectively) based on the pulley's operating speed (in $\\text{rpm}$). The data is presented for two common frequencies: $50 \\text{ Hz}$ and $60 \\text{ Hz}$.\n\n### 1. Conveyor Capacity (Torque Requirement)\n\nThis table shows the required torque (measured in $\\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}$) based on the operating speed ($\\text{rpm}$).\n\n| Operating Speed ($\\text{rpm}$) | Torque ($50 \\text{ Hz}$) ($\\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}$) | Torque ($60 \\text{ Hz}$) ($\\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}$) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 5 | $47.1$ | $56.5$ |\n| 10 | $36.4$ | $37.7$ |\n| 15 | $28.2$ | $31.4$ |\n| 20 | $22.5$ | $25.8$ |\n| 25 | $15.7$ | $18.8$ |\n| 30 | $11.3$ | $15.7$ |\n| 35 | $9.4$ | $11.3$ |\n| 40 | $7.9$ | $9.4$ |\n| 50 | $6.5$ | $7.9$ |\n| 60 | $5.7$ | $6.7$ |\n| 75 | $3.9$ | $4.7$ |\n| 90 | $3.1$ | $3.8$ |\n\n### 2. Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Speed/Torque)\n\nThis table shows the relationship between the belt speed and the required torque, providing operational guidance.\n\n| Operating Speed ($\\text{rpm}$) | Torque ($50 \\text{ Hz}$) ($\\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}$) | Torque ($60 \\text{ Hz}$) ($\\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}$) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 5 | $47.1$ | $56.5$ |\n| 10 | $36.4$ | $37.7$ |\n| 15 | $28.2$ | $31.4$ |\n| 20 | $22.5$ | $25.8$ |\n| 25 | $15.7$ | $18.8$ |\n| 30 | $11.3$ | $15.7$ |\n| 35 | $9.4$ | $11.3$ |\n| 40 | $7.9$ | $9.4$ |\n| 50 | $6.5$ | $7.9$ |\n| 60 | $5.7$ | $6.7$ |\n| 75 | $3.9$ | $4.7$ |\n| 90 | $3.1$ | $3.8$ |\n\n***\n\n## 📝 Summary of Models\n\nThe technical specifications and operational tables are **identical** for both models, suggesting they are highly interchangeable or represent a minor variation within the same product line.\n\n### 1. Model 4.3.25 CVSXE\n*   **Application:** Conveyor pulley system.\n*   **Design:** Flat belt, single belt, high power.\n*   **Features:** Central drive, $\\text{30 mm}$ pulley diameter, medium conveying length.\n\n### 2. Model 4.3.26 CVSYE\n*   **Application:** Conveyor pulley system.\n*   **Design:** Flat belt, single belt, high power.\n*   **Features:** Central drive, $\\text{30 mm}$ pulley diameter, medium conveying length.\n\n***\n\n## 🔗 Supporting Information (Further Details)\n\nThe bottom section lists associated technical documentation and resources:\n\n*   **Connection:** Further information is available for connection details.\n    *   *Source:* Page 43\n*   **Belt characteristics:** Documentation regarding belt properties.\n    *   *Source:* Page 36\n*   **Accessories:** Information on supplementary parts and accessories.\n    *   *Source:* Page 63\n\n[Page 29]\nThis document is a detailed technical datasheet presenting information for two models of full-belt conveyor systems: **4.3.27 CVSFAE** and **4.3.28 CVSFBE**. The summary below includes the product specifications, key technical data, and performance metrics.\n\n***\n\n## 📄 Detailed Summary of Conveyor Systems Datasheet\n\n### ⚙️ Product Overview and Specifications\n\nThe page features two separate conveyor models, each with distinct technical specifications (particularly concerning pulley size and general dimensions).\n\n#### 1. Model 4.3.27 CVSFAE\n*   **System Type:** Full-belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Key Components:** Pulley $\\emptyset$ 30 mm, Head drive.\n*   **Technical Data:**\n    *   **Belt Width:** 60 – 300 mm\n    *   **Length:** 280 – 2000 mm\n    *   **Weight:** 4 – 16.3 kg\n    *   **Power Output (W):** 6 – 25 W\n    *   **Voltage (V):** 230 V\n    *   **Frequency (Hz):** 50 Hz\n\n#### 2. Model 4.3.28 CVSFBE\n*   **System Type:** Full-belt conveyors, single belt.\n*   **Key Components:** Pulley $\\emptyset$ 50 mm, Head drive.\n*   **Technical Data:**\n    *   **Belt Width:** 60 – 300 mm\n    *   **Length:** 320 – 2000 mm\n    *   **Weight:** 6 – 23.9 kg\n    *   **Power Output (W):** 6 – 15 W\n    *   **Voltage (V):** 230 V\