*   **4.3.28 CVSFBE Graph:** Shows the corresponding increasing shear/bearing capacity as belt width increases, also maintaining separate curves for 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n***\n\n### ℹ️ Further Information and Documentation\n\nThe page includes standard navigational links directing the user to more detailed documentation:\n\n*   **Connection:** From page 43\n*   **Belt characteristics:** From page 36\n*   **Accessories:** From page 63\n\n[Page 30]\nThis page presents detailed technical specifications and operational guidelines for two similar conveyor belt systems manufactured by Misumi: **Model 4.3.29 CVSFCE** and **Model 4.3.30 CVSFDE**.\n\nThe summary is divided by product model, followed by a synthesis of common features and technical data.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ I. Model 4.3.29 CVSFCE (Left Side)\n\n### A. Product Overview and Diagram\nThis model features a full-belt conveyor system with a drive head and a visible pulley diameter of **30 mm**. The diagram illustrates the setup, emphasizing the belt path and the integrated drive system.\n\n### B. Special Features\n*   **Application:** Full-belt conveyors (single belt).\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\emptyset 30$ mm.\n*   **Drive System:** Head drive.\n*   **Safety/Design:** Includes a belt with meandering prevention crosspiece.\n\n### C. Technical Specifications (Table)\n| Parameter | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt width** | 70 – 300 | mm |\n| **Length** | 280 – 2000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 4 – 18.3 | kg |\n| **Power output** | 6 – 25 | W |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### D. Operational Diagrams and Data\nThe page includes two detailed graphs illustrating the performance of the conveyor system based on the Reduction Ratio.\n\n**1. Conveyor Capacity vs. Reduction Ratio**\n*   **X-Axis:** Reduction Ratio (labeled 0 to 10).\n*   **Y-Axis:** Conveyor Capacity (labeled 0 to 60).\n*   **Data Interpretation:** The curves show the relationship between reduction ratio and capacity for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz operation. The system is optimized for maintaining high capacity across a broad range of operational ratios.\n\n**2. Gearhead Reduction Ratio vs. Reduction Ratio**\n*   **X-Axis:** Reduction Ratio.\n*   **Y-Axis:** Gearhead Reduction Ratio (labeled 0 to 10).\n*   **Data Interpretation:** This curve indicates how the gearhead functions relative to the reduction ratio, ensuring consistent and efficient mechanical transmission across varying operational speeds.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ II. Model 4.3.30 CVSFDE (Right Side)\n\n### A. Product Overview and Diagram\nThis model is similar to 4.3.29 but features a larger pulley diameter of **50 mm**. The diagram shows the belt path and drive system, indicating a higher capacity setup than the 4.3.29 model.\n\n### B. Special Features\n*   **Application:** Full-belt conveyors (single belt).\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\emptyset 50$ mm.\n*   **Drive System:** Head drive.\n*   **Safety/Design:** Includes a belt with meandering prevention crosspiece.\n\n### C. Technical Specifications (Table)\n| Parameter | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt width** | 70 – 300 | mm |\n| **Length** | 280 – 2000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 6 – 23.9 | kg |\n| **Power output** | 6 – 25 | W |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### D. Operational Diagrams and Data\nThe diagrams and graphs provided for 4.3.30 CVSFDE are identical in nature to those for 4.3.29, illustrating the operational performance curves for Conveyor Capacity and Gearhead Reduction Ratio across 50 Hz and 60 Hz.\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 III. Key Data and Comparison Summary\n\n### A. Technical Comparison Table\n| Feature | 4.3.29 CVSFCE | 4.3.30 CVSFDE | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Pulley Diameter** | $\\emptyset 30$ mm | $\\emptyset 50$ mm | The primary difference, indicating a larger operational footprint/capacity. |\n| **Bolt Width Range** | 70 – 300 mm | 70 – 300 mm | Identical adaptability for mounting. |\n| **Length Range** | 280 – 2000 mm | 280 – 2000 mm | Identical operational length capability. |\n| **Weight Range** | 4 – 18.3 kg | 6 – 23.9 kg | The 4.3.30 is heavier, correlating with the larger pulley/size. |\n| **Power Output** | 6 – 25 W | 6 – 25 W | Identical operational power range. |\n| **Frequency** | 50 Hz | 50 Hz | Both models are specified for 50 Hz operation. |\n\n### B. Synthesis of Features\nBoth models are highly customizable full-belt conveyor solutions designed for industrial use. They share the following core attributes:\n1.  **Full-belt design:** Suitable for handling materials via a continuous belt.\n2.  **Safety Integration:** Both include a meandering prevention crosspiece, enhancing safety and stability.\n3.  **Drive Method:** Utilizes a Head drive system.\n4.  **Operation:** Performance data is provided for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz systems, allowing engineers to select optimal speed parameters.\n\n### C. Further Information\nThe bottom section provides consistent linking information, guiding users to technical deep dives regarding:\n*   Connection (Wiring/Setup)\n*   Belt Characteristics\n*   Accessories\n\n[Page 31]\nThis page provides a detailed technical comparison and specification guide for two models of flat belt conveyers from MISUMI: the **4.3.31 CVSJAE** and the **4.3.32 CVSMAE**.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive summary covering the product features, technical specifications, diagrams, and key data tables.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Overview of Conveyor Models\n\nThe page features two related models designed for conveying applications, differentiated by their pulley size, drive setup, and overall design.\n\n### 1. Model 4.3.31 CVSJAE\nThis model is characterized by a centralized drive and a specific pulley size, suited for general conveyor operations.\n\n**Diagram:** Shows a pulley/roller assembly with associated belt structure.\n**Special Features:**\n*   Flat belt conveyers, single belt.\n*   Pulley $\\emptyset$ 30 mm.\n*   Central drive setup.\n*   Belt includes a meandering prevention crosspiece.\n\n**Technical Data:**\n*   **Bolt width:** 50–300\n*   **Length:** 220–600\n*   **Weight:** 6.7–14.3\n*   **Power output:** 6 (Unit not specified, likely kW)\n*   **Voltage:** 230\n*   **Frequency:** 50\n\n**Key Graph: Conveyor Capacity vs. Belt Speed**\nA graph illustrates the theoretical capacity (tonnage/unit) of the conveyor belt relative to the belt speed (m/min) for both 50 Hz and 60 Hz operational frequencies. The capacity decreases significantly as belt speed increases.\n\n### 2. Model 4.3.32 CVSMAE\nThis model is a more robust or spatially efficient unit, featuring an integrated drive and a larger pulley.\n\n**Diagram:** Shows a longer, enclosed conveyor unit structure.\n**Special Features:**\n*   Flat belt conveyers, single belt, *short design*.\n*   Pulley $\\emptyset$ 70 mm.\n*   Integrated drive setup.\n*   Reduced conveyor height.\n\n**Technical Data:**\n*   **Bolt width:** 60–100, 150\n*   **Length:** 415–2000\n*   **Weight:** 6.2–18.7\n*   **Power output:** 6 (Unit not specified)\n*   **Voltage:** 230\n*   **Frequency:** 50\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Key Data Tables and Performance Data\n\n### Gearhead Reduction Ratio / Conveyor Capacity (Model 4.3.32 CVSMAE)\n\nThe second main section contains a detailed table demonstrating how the conveyor capacity changes based on the belt speed (measured in RPM) and the operational frequency (50 Hz or 60 Hz).\n\n| Speed (RPM) | 50 Hz Capacity | 60 Hz Capacity |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **5** | 47.1 | 56.5 |\n| **7.5** | 31.4 | 37.7 |\n| **12.5** | 18.8 | 22.0 |\n| **18** | 15.7 | 18.8 |\n| **25** | 13.1 | 15.7 |\n| **30** | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| **35** | 7.9 | 9.4 |\n| **50** | 5.7 | 7.9 |\n| **60** | 3.9 | 5.7 |\n| **75** | 3.1 | 3.8 |\n| **90** | 2.6 | 3.1 |\n| **120** | 2.4 | 2.8 |\n| **150** | 2.0 | 2.4 |\n| **180** | 1.8 | 2.2 |\n\n---\n\n## ℹ️ Summary of Auxiliary Information\n\nThe bottom section of the page functions as a navigational index, directing the user to related documentation:\n\n**Further Information:**\n*   **Connection:** $\\rightarrow$ from page 43\n*   **Belt characteristics:** $\\rightarrow$ from page 36\n*   **Accessories:** $\\rightarrow$ from page 63\n\n*(Note: The page number "27" suggests this summary is derived from a larger catalog document.)*\n\n[Page 32]\nThis page provides detailed specifications, diagrams, and performance curves for two models of belt conveyor systems: the **4.3.33 CVLPAE** and the **4.3.34 CVMAE**.\n\nThe summary is divided by product for clarity, ensuring all technical data, diagrams, and tables are incorporated.\n\n***\n\n## ⚙️ General Overview\n\nBoth models are designed for single-belt, flat belt conveying applications. They are highly modular, allowing for variable belt width and length. The performance of the system is analyzed using capacity and reduction ratio curves based on operating frequency (50 Hz or 60 Hz) and belt speed.\n\n***\n\n## 📑 1. Model 4.3.33 CVLPAE\n\n### **Key Features and Diagram**\n*   **Application:** Single belt, flat belt conveyor.\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\emptyset$ 15 mm.\n*   **Drive System:** Central drive.\n*   **Design:** Low design.\n*   **Diagram:** Shows the belt running over a pulley and drive mechanism.\n\n### **Technical Specifications (Table)**\n| Parameter | Specification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width (mm)** | 60–300 |\n| **Length (mm)** | 300–2000 |\n| **Power Input (W)** | 25 |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 |\n\n### **Performance Data and Curves**\n\n#### **A. Conveyor Capacity**\n*   **Diagram:** Shows Capacity (in kg) vs. Belt Speed (m/s).\n*   **Key Data Trend:** Capacity generally decreases as belt speed increases.\n*   **Capacity Table (Illustrative Data Points):**\n\n| Belt Speed (m/s) | 50 Hz (kg) | 60 Hz (kg) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 7.5 | 57 | 66 |\n| 12.5 | 45 | 54 |\n| 17.5 | 36 | 43 |\n| 22 | 28 | 33 |\n\n#### **B. Gearhead Reduction Ratio**\n*   **Diagram:** Shows Reduction Ratio vs. Belt Speed.\n*   **Key Data Trend:** The reduction ratio is stable or increases slightly as belt speed increases, maintaining the required drive torque.\n*   **Reduction Ratio Table (Illustrative Data Points):**\n\n| Belt Speed (m/s) | 50 Hz | 60 Hz |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 7.5 | 5.6 | 5.7 |\n| 12.5 | 7.3 | 7.6 |\n| 17.5 | 9.4 | 11.3 |\n| 22 | 11.3 | 12.9 |\n\n***\n\n## 📑 2. Model 4.3.34 CVMAE\n\n### **Key Features and Diagram**\n*   **Application:** Single belt, flat belt conveyor.\n*   **Pulley Diameter:** $\\emptyset$ 30 mm.\n*   **Drive System:** Head drive.\n*   **Functionality:** Selectable motor position.\n*   **Diagram:** Shows the belt running over a pulley and drive mechanism, mounted at the head end.\n\n### **Technical Specifications (Table)**\n| Parameter | Specification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width (mm)** | 50–300 |\n| **Length (mm)** | 200–2000 |\n| **Power Input (W)** | 25 |\n| **Frequency (Hz)** | 50 |\n\n### **Performance Data and Curves**\n\n#### **A. Conveyor Capacity**\n*   **Diagram:** Shows Capacity (in kg) vs. Belt Speed (m/s).\n*   **Key Data Trend:** Similar to CVLPAE, capacity decreases as speed increases.\n*   **Capacity Table (Illustrative Data Points):**\n\n| Belt Speed (m/s) | 50 Hz (kg) | 60 Hz (kg) |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 7.5 | 56 | 66 |\n| 12.5 | 44 | 53 |\n| 17.5 | 35 | 42 |\n| 22 | 27 | 32 |\n\n#### **B. Gearhead Reduction Ratio**\n*   **Diagram:** Shows Reduction Ratio vs. Belt Speed.\n*   **Key Data Trend:** The ratio is also stable, reflecting the required mechanical advantage across various operating speeds.\n*   **Reduction Ratio Table (Illustrative Data Points):**\n\n| Belt Speed (m/s) | 50 Hz | 60 Hz |\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| 7.5 | 5.4 | 5.6 |\n| 12.5 | 7.1 | 7.3 |\n| 17.5 | 9.1 | 11.0 |\n| 22 | 10.8 | 12.7 |\n\n***\n\n## 📚 Summary of Information and Links\n\nThe page concludes with standard navigational links for further detailed information:\n\n*   **Further Information:**\n    *   Connection $\\rightarrow$ from page 43\n    *   Belt characteristics $\\rightarrow$ from page 36\