 |\n| **Frequency** | 50 Hz |\n\n### **📊 Conveyor Capacity (Graph Analysis)**\nThe graph illustrates the **Conveyor Capacity** (Units: N/A, likely load capacity or power-time efficiency) based on the belt speed. Capacity decreases as the belt speed increases, showing two distinct curves for 50 Hz and 60 Hz operation.\n\n#### **Capacity Data Table**\nThis table summarizes the relationship between speed (labeled on the X-axis) and conveyor capacity for both frequencies.\n\n| Speed/Time Interval | 50 Hz Capacity | 60 Hz Capacity |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **25** | 3.2 | 3.7 |\n| **50** | 3.0 | 3.8 |\n| **75** | 2.7 | 4.1 |\n| **100** | 2.4 | 2.9 |\n| **150** | 1.8 | 2.1 |\n| **180** | 1.3 | 1.6 |\n\n---\n\n## 🔗 Part 2: 4.3.42 CVSPAE (Plastic Chain Conveyor)\n\nThis system utilizes a durable plastic chain mechanism, suitable for different material handling requirements.\n\n### **Diagram & Special Features**\n*   **Diagram:** Shows a mechanical conveyor system with guide rails and a pulley/roller mechanism.\n*   **Special Features:**\n    *   Plastic chain conveyors, double track.\n    *   Sprocket-wheel Ø 57 mm.\n    *   Head drive.\n    *   *Note:* Stoppers, sensors can be installed in the gap.\n\n### **Key Technical Data**\n| Parameter | Specification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Belt Width** | 80–300 mm |\n| **Length** | 300–3000 mm |\n| **Weight** | 9.6–27.7 kg |\n| **Power Output** | 25 W |\n| **Voltage** | 220 V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 Hz |\n\n### **📊 Gearhead Reduction Ratio (Graph Analysis)**\nThe graph illustrates the **Gearhead Reduction Ratio** as a function of belt speed. The ratio generally increases as speed decreases, indicating how efficiently the motor's speed is converted for the given belt velocity.\n\n#### **Reduction Ratio Data Table**\nThis table summarizes the reduction ratio based on the speed interval for both frequencies.\n\n| Speed/Time Interval | 50 Hz Ratio | 60 Hz Ratio |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **25** | 5.3 | 6.4 |\n| **50** | 3.7 | 4.3 |\n| **75** | 2.5 | 3.8 |\n| **100** | 1.7 | 2.1 |\n| **150** | 1.2 | 1.5 |\n| **180** | 1.0 | 1.8 |\n\n---\n\n## 📚 General Information & Specifications\n\n### **Shared Technical Specifications (General)**\nBoth models share the following standard technical parameters:\n*   **Voltage:** 220 V\n*   **Power Output:** 25 W\n\n### **Navigation and Product Index**\nThe bottom section provides index links for further technical documentation:\n*   **Connection:** From page 43\n*   **Belt characteristics:** From page 36\n*   **Accessories:** From page 63\n\n[Page 37]\nThis document provides a highly detailed comparison and specification summary for two industrial conveyor systems: the **4.3.43 CVSSAE** and the **4.3.44 CVDSAE**.\n\n***\n\n## 🚧 4.3.43 CVSSAE Conveyor System\n\nThis section details the specifications for the first conveyor model, emphasizing its specialized features and operational ranges.\n\n### ⚙️ Key Features (Special Features)\n*   **Belt:** Stainless steel belt, single belt.\n*   **Pulley:** $\\emptyset$ 50 mm.\n*   **Drive:** Head drive.\n*   **Durability:** Designed for heat resistance and conductivity.\n\n### 📊 Technical Data (Specifications)\n| Parameter | Range / Value | Unit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bolt Width** | 20–150 | mm |\n| **Length** | 250–2000 | mm |\n| **Weight** | 6.7–20.4 | kg |\n| **Power Output** | 6–25 | W |\n| **Voltage** | 220 | V |\n| **Frequency** | 50 | Hz |\n\n### 📈 Conveyor Capacity Diagram (Speed vs. Capacity)\nThe graph illustrates the achievable conveyor capacity (measured in force/capacity units) relative to the belt speed for various belt types (represented by different colored lines/labels).\n\n**Capacity Data Points (Illustrative):**\n*   The graph shows how capacity decreases as belt speed increases.\n*   Three belt types are highlighted: 125/150, 200/250, and 300/350.\n*   At a speed of 10 m/s, the available capacity ranges significantly across the different belt types.\n\n***\n\n## 🛡️ 4.3.44 CVDSAE Conveyor Syste